    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41295&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Illustration",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Visual Arts Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title : Lecturer - Illustration FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range : $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00608146 – Requisition #41295 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. In Visual Arts at CU Denver, the city becomes our canvas, industry leaders become professors and a passion becomes a profession. We do our best work designing in a digital lab or putting paint to canvas in a studio. Our students have access to state-of-the art digital labs, sculpture studios, industrial equipment and darkrooms. They find opportunities at the Denver Art Museum, in galleries across the Front Range and at digital studios like Pixar. That’s how the College of Arts & Media unites the ability to create with the means to succeed. Illustration at CU Denver has been recognized by Animation Career Review as a top national program. Traditional, conceptual, and technology-based education combine for dynamic course work that includes Image Making, Digital Illustration, Print Media, Investigative Methods, Digital Painting, Graphic Novel Workshop, Business of Art, and Typography. Illustration faculty prepare students for passionate successful careers in visual art, design, and illustration. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer - Illustration What you will do: 100% Teaching Teaching Load: You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) Instruction: Your focus will include one or more of the following areas- Illustration I: Image Making, Illustration II: Digital Media, Illustration III: Investigative Methods, Illustration IV: Thesis Development, Illustration V: BFA Thesis, Drawing 1, Life Drawing 1, Printed Image, Life Drawing 2: Portraiture & Anatomy, Life Painting and Drawing, Painting I, Media of Drawing, Drawing for Story, Digital Painting, Graphic Novel, Concept Art, Business of Art Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BFA in Illustration, Animation, Games or a related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) MFA in Illustration. Three (3) years professional experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong drawing & painting skills including perspective & anatomy. Expertise in a specialization like Children’s Books, Comics, Concept Art, Animation, Game Art, Tattooing or similar. Strong interpersonal and communication skills across multiple teaching modalities. Demonstrated history of building and maintaining effective working relationships with colleagues, students, and community partners representing a wide range of perspectives. Ability to work autonomously, taking initiative on tasks, and meeting deadlines. Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Interest in emerging trends and technologies in illustration education and practice. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training.The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 14, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications 2. Current CV or résumé Questions should be directed to charles.valsechi@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41231&lang=en": {
      "title": "Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Sep 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Faculty Fellow Working Title: Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5,000 stipend Position #00853566– Requisition #41231 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development and Advancement (CFDA) invites applications from faculty of all ranks for a Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow position. This fellowship provides an opportunity for a faculty member to collaborate with CFDA in designing, launching, and facilitating a cohort-based Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Midcareer faculty often experience a unique set of opportunities and challenges as they navigate promotion pathways, leadership opportunities, increased service responsibilities, evolving scholarly agendas, and long-term career planning. The Faculty Success Fellow will help create a structured, cohort-based experience (for Spring 2027) that supports faculty in sustaining productivity, enhancing professional fulfillment, building community, and strategically planning the next phase of their academic careers. The Fellow will have substantial autonomy and flexibility to develop programming, pilot innovative initiatives, and design experiences that address the needs of midcareer faculty while partnering closely with CFDA leadership. This position requires an estimated commitment of 5-7 hours per week during the academic year. Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow What you will do: Program Design and Development Collaborate with CFDA to create and implement a cohort-based Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Identify priority topics, goals, and outcomes for participants. Design programming that addresses areas such as: Career planning and goal setting Promotion and advancement Scholarly productivity and impact Workload management and prioritization Work-life integration and well-being Leadership development Navigating institutional culture and influence Building networks and collaborations Mentorship and sponsorship Faculty vitality and long-term career engagement Develop program materials, resources, and learning activities. Cohort Facilitation and Community Building Recruit and support faculty participation in the program. Facilitate cohort meetings, workshops, discussions, and reflective activities. Foster meaningful peer connections and interdisciplinary networking. Create opportunities for faculty to share experiences, strategies, and challenges related to midcareer development. Innovation and Faculty-Led Programming Design and pilot new initiatives that support midcareer faculty success. Develop programming aligned with their own interests, expertise, and identified faculty needs. Explore emerging best practices and current research on faculty development and career advancement. Propose innovative approaches to supporting faculty engagement, productivity, and career satisfaction. Partner with CFDA to translate successful ideas into a sustainable program for midcareer faculty of all ranks. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Develop methods for evaluating program effectiveness and participant outcomes. Collect and analyze participant feedback. Recommend program enhancements and future directions. Assist in documenting program outcomes and institutional impact. Campus Engagement and Outreach Build relationships with faculty, departments, schools, and colleges across campus. Promote participation in the Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Serve as an advocate for faculty development and career advancement. Help identify emerging needs and opportunities for supporting faculty success. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentoring, or academic career advancement. Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines and career stages. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience mentoring faculty or leading faculty development initiatives. Experience facilitating workshops, learning communities, or professional development programs. Experience in faculty leadership roles, such as program director, department chair, committee chair, or similar positions. Interest in faculty well-being, productivity, engagement, and career development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Passionate about supporting faculty success and professional growth. Bring creativity, initiative, and innovative thinking to program development. Enjoy designing and facilitating engaging learning experiences. Demonstrate strong organizational skills. Value collaboration, inclusion, and community building. Be committed to helping faculty thrive throughout their academic careers. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Position will last for one academic year Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at a $5,000 stipend. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 19, 2026 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Aubrey Thorburn, AUBREY.THORBURN@UCDENVER.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41228&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Mentorship Fellow",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Sep 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Faculty Fellow Working Title: Faculty Mentorship Fellow FTE : Part Time | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,000 stipend Position #00853564– Requisition #41228 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development and Advancement (CFDA) invites applications from faculty of all ranks for a Faculty Mentorship Fellow position. This appointment provides an opportunity for a faculty member to play a leadership role in expanding and strengthening mentoring initiatives across the University of Colorado Denver. The Faculty Mentorship Fellow will partner with CFDA to cultivate a robust culture of mentorship that supports faculty success, belonging, career advancement, and community building. While the Fellow will assist with existing mentorship initiatives, they will also have significant autonomy to develop and implement new mentoring programs, pilot innovative approaches, and help shape the future direction of faculty mentoring at CU Denver. The Fellow will work collaboratively with CFDA leadership while bringing their own expertise, ideas, and creativity to the role. Faculty who are passionate about mentoring and interested in designing meaningful programs that address emerging faculty needs are especially encouraged to apply. This position requires an estimated commitment of 5-7 hours per week during the academic year. Working Faculty Title What you will do : Mentorship Program Development and Innovation Collaborate with CFDA to expand and enhance faculty mentoring initiatives across the university. Assist with the recruitment, matching, and ongoing support of faculty mentors and mentees. Develop resources, tools, and programming that strengthen mentoring strategies, relationships, and outcomes. Identify opportunities for innovation and implement new mentoring strategies that address the evolving needs of faculty. Mentorship Circles Assist in the design, implementation, and assessment of faculty mentorship circles. Develop new mentorship circle models based on faculty interests and institutional priorities. Support and facilitate mentorship circles as needed while creating opportunities for interdisciplinary networking and peer support. Identity-Based Mentoring Initiatives Collaborate with campus partners to develop mentoring opportunities that support faculty from diverse backgrounds, identities, and career experiences. Design and implement identity-based mentoring programs that foster belonging, community, and professional growth. Explore emerging best practices and develop creative approaches to supporting faculty through mentoring networks and communities. Faculty-Led Program Development Propose and develop new mentoring programs aligned with their interests, expertise, and identified faculty needs. Pilot innovative mentoring models and evaluate their effectiveness. Collaborate with CFDA staff to translate ideas into sustainable programs and resources. Serve as a thought partner in shaping the strategic direction of mentoring efforts at CU Denver. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Collect and analyze feedback from mentoring participants. Contribute to program evaluation efforts and recommendations for future growth. Assist in documenting impacts and outcomes of mentoring initiatives. Campus Engagement and Outreach Serve as a champion for mentorship and faculty development. Promote mentoring opportunities across the institution. Build connections with faculty, departments, and campus partners to strengthen mentoring engagement. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentoring, or academic career advancement. Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines and career stages. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience mentoring faculty or leading faculty development initiatives. Experience facilitating workshops, learning communities, or professional development programs. Experience in faculty leadership roles, such as program director, department chair, committee chair, or similar positions. Interest in faculty well-being, productivity, engagement, and career development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate a strong commitment to mentoring, faculty success, and community building. Bring creativity, initiative, and a willingness to develop new programs and approaches. Enjoy collaborating with colleagues while also working independently to advance projects. Value innovation and continuous improvement in faculty development. Possess strong interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills. Be excited by the opportunity to influence mentoring culture and practices across the university. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Position will last for one academic year. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at - $5,000 stipend. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 19, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Aubrey Thorburn, AUBREY.THORBURN@UCDENVER.EDU. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41199&lang=en": {
      "title": "Dean of the Business School",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Dean Working Title: Dean of the Business School FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $260,000 - $320,000 Position # 00350380 – Requisition #41199 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at Summit Search Solutions- Dean of the Business School - University of Colorado Denver (Denver, CO) * The Dean of the Business School, reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, is responsible for serving as the chief academic officer of the school with full responsibility for its academic programs and curricula, the school’s budget, outreach and engagement with the business community, and development activities. In collaboration with the faculty, the Dean will provide intellectual leadership and a strong commitment to the School’s undergraduate and graduate programs. The Dean is expected to increase the school’s resource base by leading fundraising activities for the school, in partnership with an advancement officer. The Dean will also: strengthen engagement of and collaborations with industry and business partners; increase the amount and visibility of scholarship (research/creative work) activity of the faculty; work to promote transformation, innovation and entrepreneurial activities that will prepare the school well for the future; lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and other experiential learning activities; foster a climate that demonstrates a commitment to diversity and inclusion; develop a strong alumni network in conjunction with an enhanced focus on job placement; and demonstrate a strong commitment to the university’s urban location while exploring opportunities to engage across Colorado and around the globe. Dean of Business School What you will do: Reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the chief academic, administrative, and financial officer of the Business School. The Dean provides visionary, collaborative, and entrepreneurial leadership that advances the School's mission and aligns with the university's strategic plan. Working closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, industry partners, and university leadership, the Dean will strengthen academic excellence, expand the School's impact, foster innovation and entrepreneurship, support research production, and enhance student success and workforce outcomes. Strategic Leadership and Vision Provide bold, collaborative leadership to advance the Business School and position it for long-term success. • Develop and implement a strategic vision for the Business School that aligns with the university's refreshed strategic plan and reflects the opportunities of a leading urban research university. • Foster a culture of innovation, adaptability, and continuous improvement in response to emerging trends in business, technology, workforce development, and higher education. • Partner with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community stakeholders to identify priorities and achieve measurable outcomes. • Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and campus leaders to advance institution-wide goals and initiatives. • Serve as the chief advocate and ambassador for the Business School locally, statewide, nationally, and globally. Academic Excellence, Research, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship Advance excellence in teaching, scholarship, innovation, and entrepreneurial thinking across all programs. • Provide intellectual leadership for undergraduate, graduate, executive, and professional education programs. • Support faculty excellence in teaching, research, creative work, and community-engaged scholarship. • Increase the visibility, impact, and external funding of faculty scholarship and research. • Promote interdisciplinary collaboration and partnerships that address complex business and societal challenges. • Strengthen innovation, entrepreneurship, and experiential learning throughout the curriculum and co-curricular experience. • Ensure successful maintenance and continuous improvement of AACSB accreditation and academic quality standards. • Position the School as a leader in emerging areas such as artificial intelligence, data analytics, digital transformation, sustainability, and entrepreneurial innovation. Student Success and Career Outcomes Champion a student-centered culture that promotes access, success, belonging, and career readiness. • Lead strategies that increase enrollment, persistence, retention, graduation, and post-graduation success. • Enhance the student experience through high-impact practices, experiential learning, internships, applied projects, and global learning opportunities. • Strengthen pathways that support student achievement and social mobility. • Expand partnerships that create employment opportunities, career preparation, and professional mentorship. • Foster an inclusive learning environment where all students can thrive and achieve their educational goals. • Utilize data-informed decisionsto support enrollment management, student success, and program effectiveness. Partnerships, Advancement, and External Engagement Cultivate relationships that advance the School's reputation, impact, and resource base. • Build and strengthen strategic partnerships with business, industry, government, nonprofit, and community organizations. • Expand collaborations that support internships, workforce development, sponsored research, innovation, and entrepreneurship. • Lead fundraising efforts in partnership with University Advancement to secure philanthropic support and strategic investments. • Engage alumni as ambassadors, mentors, advisors, employers, and donors. • Enhance the visibility and reputation of the Business School through thought leadership and engagement with external stakeholders. • Leverage the university's urban location to create meaningful regional, statewide, national, and global partnerships. Organizational, Financial, and People Leadership Lead with transparency, collaboration, accountability, and a commitment to shared governance. • Oversee the School's budget, personnel, facilities, and resources to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability. • Recruit, retain, develop, and support outstanding faculty and staff. • Support department chairs and program directors in achieving academic and strategic goals. • Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, trust, shared governance, and mutual respect. • Promote excellence through clear expectations, assessment, and continuous improvement. • Advance a welcoming and inclusive environment that values diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. • Meet established goals and performance expectations while ensuring responsible stewardship of university resources. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Earned terminal degree in a discipline relevant to the Business School's academic programs. • Record of transformative leadership demonstrating the ability to develop and execute strategic priorities, lead organizational change, and achieve measurable results. • Evidence of success building partnerships with industry, government, nonprofit, and community organizations. • Demonstrated ability to secure resources through fundraising, external partnerships, sponsored programs, or other revenue-generating activities. • Proven ability to lead collaboratively and effectively in complex organizations. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Successful senior leadership experience at a research university, business school, or comparable complex organization. • Demonstrated record of advancing innovation, entrepreneurship, and interdisciplinary collaboration. • Experience leading initiatives that improve student success, enrollment growth, retention, and career outcomes. • Record of advancing inclusive excellence and fostering environments where diverse communities thrive. • Understanding of the evolving landscape of business education, including technology-enabled learning, AI, workforce partnerships, and emerging business disciplines. • Experience with strategic planning, accreditation, and organizational transformation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • A strong record of thought leadership and influence in business; credibility with business and government leaders as an innovator in business practice and education; and strong mentorship; • Exceptional visionary and strategic thinking and leadership skills; • A record of successful engagement with the business community; • Excellence in leading, evaluating, recruiting and analyzing; • Demonstrated management and administrative ability; • Effectiveness as a fundraiser, networker and strategic alliance-builder; • A commitment to diversity and inclusion; • Successful experience and/or strong potential for success building and/or enhancing strong programs of corporate sponsorships, funded research, and other mission-aligned revenue generation; • Success in establishing mutually beneficial relationships with external constituents such as, but not limited to, alumni, government, and accrediting bodies; • Excellent oral and written communication skills; • The ability to build and work with teams up and across the organization; • Demonstrable accomplishments in working with business-related constituencies that will bridge to a university setting; • A strong record demonstrating a broad working knowledge of innovation and accomplishment, entrepreneurship and technology application in business at the local, state, national and international levels; • Experience with CRM systems and data driven decision making that will translate to enrollment and marketing; • Ability to lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and experiential learning activities. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. • This position is for a three-year appointment. A review will be conducted during the third year to determine reappointment. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $260,000 - $320,000. For candidates considering a move, relocation assistance may be available. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 10, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: Summit Search Solutions- Dean of the Business School - University of Colorado Denver (Denver, CO) and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Lyndi Hewitt, lhewitt@summitsearchsolutions.com Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41193&lang=en": {
      "title": "Dean, School of Public Affairs",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Dean Working Title: Dean, School of Public Affairs FTE: Full Time 1.0 FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $235,000 - $275,000 Position #00611800– Requisition #41193 Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at: https://www.imsearch.com/open-searches/university-colorado-denver-school-public-affairs/dean Dean, School of Public Affairs Strategic Leadership and Vision Provide bold, collaborative leadership to advance the School of Public Affairs and position it for long-term success. • Develop and implement a strategic vision for the School of Public Affairs that aligns with the university's refreshed strategic plan and reflects the opportunities of a leading urban research university. • Foster a culture of innovation, adaptability, and continuous improvement in response to emerging issues in public policy, public administration, social equity, governance, nonprofit leadership, criminal justice, public finance, and civic engagement. • Partner with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community stakeholders to identify priorities and achieve measurable outcomes. • Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and campus leaders to advance institution-wide goals and initiatives. • Serve as the chief advocate and ambassador for the School of Public Affairs locally, statewide, nationally, and globally. • Position the School as a thought leader in addressing complex public challenges facing cities, states, nations, and communities. Academic Excellence, Research, and Public Impact Advance excellence in teaching, scholarship, policy engagement, and public service. • Provide intellectual leadership for undergraduate, graduate, and professional education programs. • Support faculty excellence in teaching, research, creative work, policy engagement, and community-engaged scholarship. • Increase the visibility, impact, and external funding of faculty scholarship and research. • Promote interdisciplinary collaboration and partnerships that address pressing public challenges and inform public decision-making. • Support applied research, policy analysis, and evidence-based solutions that contribute to the public good. • Ensure successful maintenance and continuous improvement of NASPAA accreditation and academic quality standards. • Strengthen the School's national reputation and ranking as a leading school of public affairs. • Advance scholarship and educational programs in areas such as public policy, public administration, nonprofit management, criminal justice, public budgeting and finance, sustainability, governance, technology and society, public health policy, and social equity. • Foster partnerships among faculty, research centers, policymakers, and practitioners to translate knowledge into action and public impact. Student Success and Leadership Development Champion a student-centered culture that promotes access, success, belonging, and preparation for public leadership. • Lead strategies that increase enrollment, persistence, retention, graduation, and post-graduation success. • Prepare students for impactful careers across government, nonprofit, philanthropic, international, and public-serving organizations. • Enhance the student experience through experiential learning, internships, capstone projects, community-engaged learning, and public service opportunities. • Strengthen pathways that support student achievement, leadership development, and social mobility. • Expand partnerships that create employment opportunities, policy fellowships, public service experiences, and professional mentorship. • Foster an inclusive learning environment where all students can thrive and achieve their educational goals. • Utilize data-informed decisions to support enrollment management, student success, and program effectiveness. • Promote civic engagement, ethical leadership, and a lifelong commitment to public service. Partnerships, Advancement, and External Engagement Cultivate relationships that advance the School's reputation, impact, and resource base. • Build and strengthen strategic partnerships with local, state, federal, and international government agencies; nonprofit organizations; philanthropic foundations; community organizations; and private-sector partners. • Expand collaborations that support research, policy innovation, experiential learning, workforce development, and community impact. • Serve as a visible and trusted leader in policy, civic, and community conversations that advance the public good. • Lead fundraising efforts in partnership with University Advancement to secure philanthropic support and strategic investments. • Engage alumni as ambassadors, mentors, advisors, practitioners, and donors. • Enhance the visibility and reputation of the School through thought leadership, public engagement, and professional association involvement. • Leverage the university's urban location and proximity to the seat of state government to create meaningful regional, statewide, national, and global partnerships. • Support executive education, professional development, and community-facing programs that serve public sector and nonprofit leaders. Organizational, Financial, and People Leadership Lead with transparency, collaboration, accountability, and a commitment to shared governance. • Oversee the School's budget, personnel, facilities, and resources to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability. • Recruit, retain, develop, and support outstanding faculty and staff. • Support center directors and program leaders in achieving academic, research, and strategic goals. • Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, trust, shared governance, and mutual respect. • Promote excellence through clear expectations, assessment, and continuous improvement. • Advance a welcoming and inclusive environment that values diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. • Support faculty and staff development while fostering a culture of engagement, innovation, and high performance. • Meet established goals and performance expectations while ensuring responsible stewardship of university resources. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • A terminal degree in a relevant discipline offered by the School of Public Affairs, from an accredited institution. • Record of transformative leadership demonstrating the ability to develop and execute strategic priorities, lead organizational change, and achieve measurable results. • Evidence of success building partnerships with government, nonprofit, and community organizations. • Demonstrated ability to successfully secure resources through fundraising, external partnerships, sponsored programs, or other revenue-generating activities. • Proven ability to lead collaboratively and effectively in complex organizations. • Substantial financial management experience, including the equitable allocation of resources across multiple programs and initiatives, and supporting innovation around new degrees, certificates, or other revenue generators. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Successful senior leadership experience at a research university, school of public affairs, or comparable complex organization. • Demonstrated record of advancing innovation and interdisciplinary collaboration. • Experience leading initiatives that improve student success, enrollment growth, retention, and career outcomes. • An innovative, intellectually engaged leader who makes difficult decisions with reflection, fairness, and transparency and is willing to challenge the status quo to guide the college to further prominence locally, nationally, and internationally. • A clear, transparent, empathetic, and empowering communication style; an openness to listening and integrating the input of others; an ability to advocate for the college's priorities; an ability to convey the mission, vision, and impact of the college and university to both internal and external audiences; and the capacity to serve as a thought leader within Colorado and beyond. • A champion for inclusive excellence, access and campus engagement with exemplary skills in communicating, collaborating with, and supporting a diverse community, removing barriers to inclusion, promoting student voice, and valuing student agency. • Ability to foster a deep sense of community both internally at the college and externally with partners; desire to listen and learn and to serve as a visible and positive presence at the school and on campus; and ability to foster a culture and community where kindness, humility, and respect are high priorities. • A relationship-based leadership style that values teamwork and collaboration; a firm belief in shared governance and a high level of collegiality in working with faculty, staff, and students; experience bringing people together to solve challenges and seize opportunities; ability to delegate; respect and appreciation for all of the disciplines of the college; and experience facilitating strong partnerships among academic programs and other divisions of the university. • A leadership style that demonstrates accountability, integrity, compassion, empathy, kindness, humility, curiosity, enthusiasm, humor, flexibility, forward-thinking, good judgment, and discernment. • A deep appreciation for research and scholarly endeavors, a record of recruiting and developing both people and programs of the highest quality. • Successful experience in or a demonstrated capacity for fundraising; an eagerness to build relationships with donors, alumni, and community partnerships to help advance the mission of SPA. • Familiarity with the issues and opportunities across a range of academic areas and a natural curiosity about a broad range of intellectual endeavors, including those represented throughout the college’s programs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Credibility with community and government leaders as a thought leader and innovator in industry practice and education Exceptional visionary and strategic thinking and leadership skills. • Excellence in leading, evaluating, recruiting and analyzing. • Demonstrated management and administrative ability. • Effectiveness as a fundraiser, networker and strategic alliance-builder. • Strong, demonstrated commitment and accomplishment in inclusive excellence, access and campus engagement. • Successful experience and/or strong potential for success building and/or enhancing strong programs of corporate sponsorships, funded research, and other mission-aligned revenue generation. • Success in establishing mutually beneficial relationships with internal and external constituents such as, but not limited to, alumni, government, and accrediting bodies. • Excellent oral and written communication skills. • The ability to build and work with teams up and across the organization. • The ability to resolve conflict in a positive manner. • Demonstrable accomplishments in working with a variety of teams, groups, and leaders that will bridge to a university setting. • Experience with data driven decision making that translates to enrollment and marketing. • Ability to lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and experiential learning activities. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. • This position is for a three-year appointment. A review will be conducted during the third year to determine reappointment. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $235,000 - $275,000 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline • Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 5th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: https://www.imsearch.com/open-searches/university-colorado-denver-school-public-affairs/dean Questions should be directed to Janette Martinez, jmartinez@imsearch.com Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41101&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 15, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Computer SC & Engineering Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Assistant Professor Working Title: Assistant Professor FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $90,000 - $125,000 Position #00636050– Requisition #41101 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Computer Science and Engineering Department (CSE) currently has sixteen full-time faculty members. The department offers a ABET accredited Bachelor of Science degree in Computer Science, a Bachelor of Arts degree in Computer Science, a Bachelor of Science degree in Cybersecurity, a Master of Science degree in Computer Science, and two multidisciplinary PhD degrees in Computer Science and Information Systems and Engineering and Applied Science, and several certificates. The CSE department provides quality computer science education and research opportunities to our students and quality professional service to the professional community and the general public in the Denver metropolitan area. The current strengths of the faculty are in the areas of algorithms, artificial intelligence, computer networks, graphics, parallel and distributed systems, mobile systems, machine learning, Cybersecurity and secure computing, data science and AI, and theory. Our faculty are engaged in multidisciplinary research and encourage collaborative research among disciplines. In addition to general computing labs, the department houses several specialized research labs in Next Generation Networking & Security, Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS), Active Cyber Infrastructure and Defense (ACID), Machine Learning (ML), networks (DECENT), Big Data Management & Mining Laboratory (BDLab), Animation, Neuroscience & AI, and parallel and distributed systems (PDS). The College of Engineering, Design and Computing values innovation, creativity and an interdisciplinary approach to engineering and research. We focus on providing our students with a comprehensive engineering education at the undergraduate, graduate and professional level. Faculty conduct research that spans our five disciplines of civil, electrical and mechanical engineering, bioengineering, and computer science and engineering. The college collaborates with industry from around the state; our laboratories and research opportunities give students the hands-on experience they need to excel in the professional world. Assistant Professor What you will do: The Department of Computer Science and Engineering in the College of Engineering, Design and Computing at the University of Colorado Denver invites applications for Assistant Professor. Reporting to the Chair of the Computer Science and Engineering Department, these positions will be expected to develop and teach lecture and laboratory courses at all levels; establish an active externally funded research program; conduct high quality research involving students at all levels, leading to sponsored research and refereed publications; advise students; and contribute to Department, College, and University governance and to the profession. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Ph.D. in Computer Science or closely related field. • Demonstrated expertise and track record of research and teaching accomplishments commensurate with the candidate’s rank in computer science, as evidenced by their record. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • While candidates in all areas of computer science will be considered, the areas of AI, Quantum Computing (including Quantum Machine Learning), Health Informatics and Technologies, Intelligent Systems, Cybersecurity, Edge Computing, Computer Vision and Cyber-Physical Systems, and/or a related field will be given priority. Conditions of Employment • These positions may follow a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preference. Working from the office is required for teaching, student interactions, committee work, and other responsibilities. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • These positions may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. • These positions may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position may be eligible now and in the future for certain visa sponsorship limited to Change of Status (COS) within the United States or if the candidate meets the criteria for the portability provision. While the hiring unit may be willing to pursue certain visa sponsorship, an offer of employment will be contingent on the candidate having a visa status that allows employment with the University as of the start date for the position or the University’s petition being approved and on the candidate being able to obtain the appropriate visa status. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at: $90,000 - $125,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline • Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by November 27, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • One (1) PDF containing the following documents combined (may not exceed 2.5 megabytes): o A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. o Statement of teaching philosophy, experience, and interests (3-page limit). o Statement of research philosophy, experience, and interests (3-page limit). o List of three professional references including name, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting references). Questions should be directed to Kelly Konrad, kelly.p.konrad@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41049&lang=en": {
      "title": "Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SEHD DEAN Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Senior Professional Working Title: Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $54,256 - $59,968 Position #00649345– Requisition #41049 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Jobs in this career family provide direct professional support for the teaching and/or educational service mission of the university. Functions include academic advising/counseling, student personnel administration, recruitment and admissions, registration, financial aid, faculty affairs, library services, curriculum administration, and others involving direct support of the educational mission of an academic unit. The School of Education and Human Development (SEHD) and its Academic Services and Continuing & Professional Education Offices are committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse student body. Nature of Work The Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator is a shared position between the Academic Services department and the Continuing & Professional Education (CPE) office in the School of Education and Human Development. In Academic Services this position manages admissions, course planning, registration and enrollment, student services, progress tracking, and graduation certification for graduate programs. CPE is an entrepreneurial unit that offers a wide range of self-funded courses and programs for working teachers and other education professionals, as well as for adults preparing for careers in education, mental health or supporting educational enterprises. This position will work with districts and partner organizations to provide student advising and program support, and will manage the implementation of both degree and non-degree programs. Additionally, the Coordinator provides administrative support to faculty, students, and staff. Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator What you will do: Recruitment and Admissions • Provides proactive, personalized, and integrated engagement to prospective students, primarily through phone and digital outreach, in a fast-paced environment, with a focus on connecting potential students to appropriate academic and student support resources. • Recruit, follow-up, and facilitate admission for students, from initial inquiry through enrollment, including students in partnership-based cohort programs. • Help students understand their estimated cost of attendance and financial aid and scholarship opportunities. • Coordinate, plan and participate in information sessions, recruitment activities, interview days, orientations, etc. • Provide oversight and advisement of applicants on admission requirements and support prospective students through the online application system. • Provide wrap-around services which include support related to financial aid, student services, and academic resources available on campus. • Facilitate the processing of applications by managing communication, materials and eligibility criteria; provides timely feedback regarding the status of applications. • Verifies transcript information, such as credits, cumulative GPA, and awarded degrees. • Tracks new student acceptance and update the student listservs. Program Coordination • Maintains a detailed multi-year course schedule to ensure students can complete their requirements. • Coordinates and communicates important deadlines. • Helps students and faculty navigate multiple academic calendars, policies and platforms. • Distributes registration information to students each term appropriate for their cohort/concentration/program of study. • Maintains confidential academic records, uploads data into student information systems, and uses advising and reporting tools to ensure accuracy. • Tracks student progress for retention. • Oversees the processes related to leaves of absence, program discontinuation, transfers, withdrawals, and academic probation for students. • Perform graduation audits when students apply to graduate and certify graduation. • Track and determine student completion of certificate and degree programs, and assist with efforts to recruit continuing and professional education non-degree students into degree programs. • Processes student forms and routes as necessary to campus administrative offices. • Supports students as they navigate the administrative aspects of the enrollment process, including those connected to admissions, financial aid, registration, and bursar functions. • Supports in-person and virtual activities; assists with catering, vendor arrangements, event and program logistics. • Assists with all university-wide commencement preparations and day-of activities. • Ensures student handbooks are updated annually and posted to the SEHD website and distributed to faculty and students. • Coordinate program activities, to include communication with program faculty, program oversight team, partner organization representatives/design team, student services, and CPE to ensure timely and efficient registration, evaluation, grading, and billing for the CPE programs. • Manage graduate faculty appointment process for CPE lecturers. • Work with instructors and program leaders to ensure that course and instructor documentation is current and accurate; that required processes, such as course evaluations and grades are completed; and that courses are scheduled according to required university timelines. Administration • Maintains files on current students including program of study, progress to degree, and other documentation related to student progress. • Maintains contact information for prospects, current students, and alumni. • Collaborates and liaises with faculty. • Organize team meetings, shared calendars, activities, and retreats. • Reviews website material related to programs to identify areas in need of revision or update. • Responsible for other duties as assigned. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time based on business needs. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Primary work hours are 8:00AM – 5:00PM Monday-Friday, and some evening/weekend activities may be required. The primary work location is the CU Denver campus, but some partial remote work options are available. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education. • One (1) year of experience working in higher education in either recruitment, admissions, advising, financial aid, or student support services. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in education in student affairs, or related field is highly desired. • Two years of extensive, diverse and progressively responsible experience, including direct responsibility for program coordination and management. • Proficient in Microsoft Office, Zoom, Slate, student information systems, and other platforms. Competencies • Demonstrated initiative and ability to work as part of a team. • Exceptional customer service skills • Able to communicate well and build rapport quickly with students, faculty, and staff. • Ability to work independently and with interdepartmental teams on various initiatives. • Excellent organization and time management skills, including the ability to set and meet goals and deadlines, manage appointments, create schedules, coordinate and facilitate meetings, and make decisions. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $54,256 - $59,968. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 24th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to SEHD HR at sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41047&lang=en": {
      "title": "Crisis Counseling Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-HWAS Stdnt&CommCounslng Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Health Care Manager Working Title: Crisis Counseling Manager FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $84,206 - $93,070 Position #00691789 – Requisition #41047 About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state’s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Crisis Counseling Manager is a licensed mental health professional within the CU Denver Student and Community Counseling Center and reports to the Assistant Director at the Counseling Center. This position provides leadership for the Counseling Center's crisis services program and is responsible for ensuring timely, coordinated, and effective responses to students experiencing acute mental health concerns and elevated levels of risk. The Crisis Counseling Manager oversees the assessment, triage, case coordination, and follow-up of high-risk students while maintaining continuity of care across university and community systems. This role collaborates closely with campus partners including Disability Resources and Services, Student Conduct and Community Standards, the Office of Case Management, faculty, International Student Services, the Ombuds Office, Auraria Health Center, and other stakeholders to support student wellbeing and safety. The Crisis Counseling Manager develops and maintains crisis response protocols, risk management procedures, referral pathways, and systems for tracking and coordinating care for students identified as high risk. The position facilitates transitions to higher levels of care when student needs exceed the Counseling Center's scope of practice and supports successful reintegration to campus following hospitalization, medical leave, or other significant mental health events. The Crisis Counseling Manager provides consultation to students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and community providers regarding complex mental health concerns and crisis response. In addition to program leadership responsibilities, the Crisis Counseling Manager provides culturally responsive clinical services, including crisis intervention, brief individual counseling, group counseling, case management, intake assessment, consultation, outreach, and prevention programming. The position also develops and delivers training and educational programs for campus stakeholders regarding student mental health, crisis response, and wellbeing promotion. The Crisis Counseling Manager supervises crisis counseling staff, contributes to the training and development of clinical trainees, and participates in departmental meetings, university committees, and collaborative initiatives that support student success and wellbeing. Based on a total of 100% of time, this position will be responsible for approximately: 40% Coordination of Crisis Services 30% Counseling Services (includes on-call) 10% Administrative (e.g., staff meeting, team meeting, trainee review, high-risk) 15% supervision and practicum student training 5% outreach and prevention services Crisis Counseling Manager What you will do: • Lead and coordinate the Counseling Center's crisis services program, including policy and procedure development, service design, workflow management, staffing plans, clinician coverage, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. • Provide clinical and administrative supervision, performance management, consultation, and professional development for crisis counseling staff. • Oversee training activities related to crisis counseling for clinical staff, trainees, and practicum students. • Provide drop-in crisis assessment and intervention services; coordinate care for students experiencing acute distress through consultation, case management, collaboration with campus partners, and referral to community resources when appropriate. • Develop and maintain systems for triage, referral management, case tracking, documentation, and follow-up of students identified as high risk. • Consult with students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and community providers regarding complex mental health concerns, crisis response, hospitalization follow-up, and return-to-campus planning. • Provide culturally responsive brief counseling, crisis intervention, group counseling, case management, and outreach services to a diverse student population. • Monitor and evaluate crisis services utilization, outcomes, and operational effectiveness; use data to inform program improvements and resource planning. • Represent the Counseling Center on multidisciplinary teams addressing students of concern, behavioral risk, and university crisis response efforts. • Participate in recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and training of crisis services staff. • Develop and deliver trainings, workshops, and consultations for campus stakeholders on mental health, crisis response, and student wellbeing; participate in departmental meetings, committees, and outreach initiatives. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) • Master’s degree in counseling-related field from an accredited institution. • Licensure as mental health professional in Colorado (LPC, LMFT, LCSW). • At least three (3) years of related professional level experience Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Experience with crisis management, including assessment, intervention, stabilization, and disposition planning. • Experience coordinating care for individuals requiring involuntary mental health evaluation, hospitalization, or higher levels of care, including related assessment, consultation, coordination, and documentation. • History of work in acute settings, such as crisis phone lines, hospital settings, behavioral health/primary care, inpatient treatment facilities, drop-in crisis centers, crisis stabilization units, etc. • Experience providing clinical supervision, consultation, or support to mental health professionals and trainees. • Experience coordinating, developing, or managing clinical programs or services. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. • Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships across the institution. • Demonstrated commitment to equitable, inclusive, and culturally responsive clinical practice. • Ability to provide culturally responsive crisis intervention and brief therapy to a diverse student population. • Ability to assess, manage, and respond effectively to students experiencing acute mental health crises. • Ability to conduct suicide, homicide, and behavioral threat risk assessments. • Ability to provide rapid assessment, triage, stabilization, and referral services in a fast-paced clinical environment. • Ability to collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary treatment team. • Ability to consult with campus and community partners regarding students of concern. • Ability to coordinate care across campus and community systems. • Ability to provide clinical and operational leadership for a crisis services program, including team coordination, workflow management, staff support, program development, and continuous quality improvement. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $84,206 - $93,070. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by priority deadline of September 27th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Dr. Matthew Heermann, matthew.heermann@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41040&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/08/2026 Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Political Science Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE : Part-time Salary Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). Position #00007258– Requisition #41040 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Political Science courses in designated fields of the discipline, which may include specializations in areas such as Area Studies, American Political Thought, Research Methodology, Constitutional Law, Environmental Politics, Labor, Social Economy, Local Government Leadership, Community Organizing/Development, and courses within their area of expertise, for the Department of Political Science in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. The Center for New Directions in Politics & Policy is within the Department of Political Science and manages an applied Master's Degree and several undergraduate and graduate certificates, delivered primarily through weekend intensive in-person graduate courses. New Directions will also hire lecturers from this pool of applicants. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The Department of Political Science will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Working Faculty Title What you will do: Teach one or two courses in the Political Science Department. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s Degree in political Science or related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Discipline related certifications PhD or ABD in Political Science. Experience teaching in a higher education environment in related field to teaching assignment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in one or more of the related teaching assignment(s). Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. Strong commitment to student education and success. Experience in online or hybrid delivery. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Sept. 9, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Please detail your availability in your letter, including the specific days (Monday-Friday, weekends) and times (daytime or evening) you are able to teach. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Kayla Spencer, kayla.spencer@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=37723&lang=en": {
      "title": "Substance Use Disorder Treatment Counselor (Entry – Senior Level)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH-ARTS SP/G Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus School of Medicine | Department of Psychiatry | Addiction Research & Treatment Services (ARTS) | Adult Outpatient Program Job Title: Substance Use Disorder Treatment Counselor (Entry – Senior Level) Position: #00730526 – Requisition: #37723 Job Summary: The Substance Use Disorder (SUD) Treatment Counselor provides drug and alcohol assessment, psychosocial, and pharmacological treatment to adults who are living with SUD. This clinical position is responsible for performing counseling duties and will be supervised by a senior counselor, a Clinical Team Lead, and/or the Clinic Manager. This position will primarily work with patients who are participating in Medication Assisted Treatment (MAT), referred from criminal justice programs, recovery courts, probation departments, and/or other referral sources (i.e. department of social services). This position is required to share on-call and Saturday coverage duties. Evening hours may be necessary as well. Some positions are morning shifts (6:00am-2:30pm) and others may be day/afternoon shifts (10:30am-7:00pm). Key Responsibilities: Provide assessments of clients for admission to treatment. Perform SUD evaluations. Complete patient intakes (new, returning, internal transfer, external transfer, etc.). Perform group, individual and family counseling. Use evidence-based practices for treating offenders and criminal-justice involved populations. Maintain accurate and timely documentation in patient charts. Develop and carry out individualized treatment plans and case management duties as needed to meet the needs of external sources as well as linking client's treatment progress to referral sources. Complete monthly billing report and statistics. Assess and collect fees from clients. Staff on-call shift rotations. Coverage of clinic front desk as needed. Work closely with problem solving courts, the Veterans Administration, Department of Social Services/Human Services, and/or other referral sources. Performing other work as assigned or required. Work Location: Onsite – this role is expected to work onsite at Adult Outpatient Clinics or the ARTS Medication Mobile Unit across the greater Metro Denver area. Why Join Us: Adult Outpatient Clinics for CU’s ARTS team are leading the fight against substance use disorder (SUD) in the state. We have several clinics across the greater Metro Denver area including in Arvada, central Denver, and Aurora. Additionally, we have a new Medication Mobile Unit which delivers medication assisted treatments to the patients of our city. We are hiring across all locations. Joining this team not only sets you up for a long-term career within the university but also makes a lasting impact in our community. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Certified Addictions Specialist (CAS), Licensed Professional Counselor Candidate (LPC-C), Social Worker Candidate (SW-C), Licensed Addiction Counselor Candidate (LAC-C), or Marriage and Family Therapist Candidate (MFT-C). Intermediate Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional level experience in Mental Health, Behavioral Health or closely related field, case management, research of Mental Health, Behavioral Health, or closely related field. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Certified Addictions Specialist (CAS), Licensed Professional Counselor Candidate (LPC-C), Social Worker Candidate (SW-C), Licensed Addiction Counselor Candidate (LAC-C), or Marriage and Family Therapist Candidate (MFT-C). Senior Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years of professional level experience in Mental Health, Behavioral Health or closely related field, case management, research of Mental Health, Behavioral Health, or closely related field. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW), Licensed Social Worker (LSW), Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC), Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) or Licensed Addiction Counselor (LAC). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Experience working in a counselor role with clients who are involved with probation, human services, social services, criminal justice programs, and/or other referral sources. Experience conducting, leading, or co-leading group counseling sessions. Experience working in a counselor role with opioid-dependent, adult clients. Experience conducting individual and/or family counseling. Experience creating individualized treatment plans and other clinical documentation (for example, DAP notes). Experience with therapeutic confrontation and structures. Experience observing, monitoring, and intervening in drug/alcohol treatment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Excellent written communication skills, which includes the ability to check for typographical, grammatical, and spelling errors. Ability to effectively manage difficult behaviors. Ability to engage patients in treatment for substance use disorder treatment. Ability to comply with established rules, policies and procedures and meet deadlines. Ability to be open-minded and nonjudgmental. Ability to develop healthy relationships with clients. Ability to establish boundaries with clients. Ability to exercise discretion (e.g. patient confidentiality). Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment: Must agree to undertake and successfully pass a fingerprint check. Must agree to undertake and successfully pass a criminal background check, professional references check, and motor vehicle records check. Must possess and maintain current and valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) to provide behavioral health treatment and care to patients throughout employment in this position. Must possess a valid driver’s license to operate a motor vehicle in Colorado or obtain one within 30 days from date of hire. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Heidi McKinnon, heidi.mckinnon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $56,555 – $71,939 Intermediate Level: $61,546 – $78,286 Senior Level: $66,536 – $84,634 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41035&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instructor - ICB",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Communication Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Instructor Working Title: Instructor - ICB FTE: Full-time, 0.9 (90%) FTE | On Site in Bejing, China Salary Range : $54,000 - $56,692 Position #00637374– Requisition #41035 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Located in the Haidian District of Beijing, International College Beijing (ICB) is an international partnership between China Agricultural University (CAU) and the University of Colorado Denver that offers complete undergraduate programs in Economics and Communication. All courses are administered and taught by CU Denver faculty in English, and the degree earned is awarded by CU Denver. The ICB program offers a thriving and collegial environment that strives to embody the best promises of international education. For more information about the CU Denver/ICB program, please see the International College Beijing web site: https://www.ucdenver.edu/offices/international-affairs/partners/international-college-beijing. What this position offers: initial airline ticket to Beijing is covered by the university and a $2,500 moving allowance is provided, payable once you start. After the initial ticket, an additional allowance is provided to purchase tickets to and from Beijing. Employees receive generous health benefits through Blue Cross Blue Shield with access to top private, English-speaking clinics in Beijing and minimal out-of-pocket costs. U.S. citizens may further qualify for a 100% return of all paid state and federal income taxes. Housing options include free guesthouse apartments (inclusive of all utilities) with private rooms, private showers, shared laundry and kitchen, as well as a gym; or heavily subsidized off-campus housing (within 200ft of campus) that offers spacious 3-bedroom, 2-bath apartments, with a sunroom and city views at higher levels of accommodation. All housing has free maintenance and upkeep. China Agricultural University, whose campus ICB is located on, is nationally famous for its outstanding food offerings – this includes multiple canteens and food vendors across campus that offer highly subsidized, delicious and nutritious food, including a Halal restaurant. At ICB, semesters are 12 to 14 weeks long; semester start dates are based on the lunar calendar with fall semesters beginning early to mid-September, and spring semesters beginning mid-February to early March. Summar and Winter semester teaching may be available for additional pay. Communication courses are offered Mon-Thurs, with no classes on Fridays, which offers opportunities to explore Beijing and its surroundings. As an ancient and modern city, Beijing offers all the amenities of a major U.S. or international city. It has excellent public transportation (including subway, highspeed rail, low-cost taxis, and two major airports) that make getting around town and travel convenient. ICB also provides faculty with professional development funds towards research and/or pedagogy, and offers free Chinese language courses. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire. The University does not have direct authority to hire Chinese citizens working in China. Faculty hired to teach at ICB must be able to meet the requirements to obtain the Z Visa to work in China ( http://english.gov.cn/services/workinchina/ ). Our understanding of these requirements includes: prior to the position start date, international (non-Chinese) candidates must hold their Master’s degree or above and have worked full-time for at least two years in a relevant area after receiving their Bachelor’s degree, or begin their appointment at ICB within 12 months of obtaining their Ph.D. Under these Chinese rules, the maximum age of candidates seeking a work Visa is 59. These requirements are subject to change by the Chinese government without notice. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Department of Communication invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track teaching position at the International College of Beijing (ICB). The job will commence in Beijing in Spring 2027. Depending on the performance of the individual hired and other circumstances, multi-year renewals are possible. We seek to hire a colleague who can teach a wide array of Communication courses across Health Communication, Digital Media, and humanistic approaches to AI, supporting one or more of the Department’s pathways and certificates, especially in health communication, strategic communication, and/or AI and human communication. This may include courses such as Interpersonal Communication, Communication Research & Writing, Communication & Citizenship, Health Communication, and Digital Health Narratives, among others. We are particularly interested in a colleague who is well-versed in incorporating the use of AI tools and/or critically examines AI’s broader societal impacts. We similarly seek a colleague who is experienced in integrating workplace readiness elements into their course design to prepare students for the workforce. The teaching load is 8 courses per academic year (4 in fall and 4 in spring) and will also assume 10% of their duties in service roles assigned in consultation with the ICB Director, Department Chair, and Associate Program Chair. These service roles may include advising students on the communication major, minor, and certificates; serving as faculty advisor or director of student clubs; contributing to or overseeing annual student festivals and ceremonies; contributing to newsletters and outcomes assessment; and other tasks. Instructor - ICB What you will do: Teach 8 courses per academic year (4 in fall and 4 in spring) Service duties assigned in consultation with the Department Chair, ICB Director, and Associate Program Chair Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree in Communication or a closely allied field (English-medium) Two years independent teaching experience as the instructor of record (English-medium) Evidence of highly effective teaching Evidence of multifaceted and excellent service to an academic department Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Ph.D. in Communication (or a closely allied discipline) Demonstrated experience in communication in U.S.-China contexts Demonstrated experience in incorporating AI tools in student assignments and assessments Demonstrated experience integrating workplace readiness and/or career preparation elements into student assignments and assessments Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficient skills in instructional technology, digital and social media environments, as well as AI/media production tools (for example, Canvas, ChatGPT, DeepSeek, Adobe, PowerPoint, Canva, and others) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, in a variety of institutional contexts. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students and employees at all levels throughout the institution. Ability to live and work in Beijing as a CU Denver employee Conditions of Employment Required to work in China for this position. Faculty hired to teach at ICB must be able to meet the requirements to obtain the Z Visa to work in China (http://english.gov.cn/services/workinchina/) To be paid via CU Denver payroll, you must have a social security number and a U.S. bank account for direct deposit CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $54,000 - $56,692. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 20, 2026. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). A single PDF file providing evidence for (a) at least two years independent teaching experience as the instructor of record (English-medium), (b) highly effective teaching, and (c) multifaceted and excellent service to an academic department. Questions should be directed to Dr. Mia Fischer, Associate Professor, Department of Communication, CU Denver, mia.fischer@ucdenver.ed u. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41031&lang=en": {
      "title": "Veteran Transition and Support Senior Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCRESS VeteranStudSrvc Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Student Services Senior Professional Working Title: Veteran Transition and Support Senior Coordinator FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $55,322 - $61,146 Position #00709287 – Requisition #41031 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Under the direction of the Director of the Office of Veteran & Military Student Services (VMSS), this position will include developing a comprehensive faculty and staff training, developing peer support programs, developing internal and external communication materials, developing, and maintaining participant tracking, developing programming and workshops in coordination with other University services (ex. Career Center, Experiential Learning) to provide job readiness and transition skills. This position will create new programming and support and oversee existing programming and support for veterans and military-connected students and will work with campus partners in creating and implementing these programs. This position will create and maintain program information materials, such as brochures, flyers, and newsletters. This position will perform outreach to existing and potential students to provide information and resources. This position will perform outreach to build and maintain strategic community partnerships. Veteran Transition & Support Senior Coordinator: What you will do: • Coordinate all VMSS program activities, events, and programs. • Serve as a resource for all military-connected students seeking education and career transition services. • Coordinate internship and career portions of the program with appropriate internal programs. • Coordinate the mentorship aspect of the program, including, but not limited to, maintaining the roster of students and professional mentors, matching them according to major (student) and career/field (mentor), introducing/connecting the student and mentor as well as monitoring the mentorship process. • Under the direction of the Director, this position will serve as a point person on Boots to Suits related issues and serve as a community liaison to local businesses/corporations, veteran organizations, and community resources. • This position will assist and be present in all Boots to Suits courses. • Coordinate services with other University Departments, specifically the CU Denver Experiential Learning and Career Centers, and others as needed. • Monitor Boots to Suits student program participants as they matriculate through the program. • Oversee the creation and continuation of all Boots to Suits promotional materials, social media information and program website. • Maintain and foster new relationships internal and external relationships with various veteran serving organizations to further develop resources for CU Denver students. • Develop and maintain a roster of CU Denver Veteran Alumni and contact them for potential future mentorship opportunities. • Perform outreach in both the CU Denver student veteran population as well as the local business community to generate more student and business interest and participation. • Develop and administer staff and facility training programs. • Oversee peer-to-peer mentor development and programing. • Serve as advisor/liaison for student veteran affiliated campus organizations. • All other duties or unforeseen responsibilities regarding the program as needed. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • A bachelor’s degree in education, communication, social science, business, public administration, business administration, higher education, counseling, liberal arts, finance, accounting, human services, student affairs, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. • Two (2) years of professional level experience working in higher education. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Veteran of the United States Armed Forces. • Master’s degree in progress or completed. • One year or more experience working with Veterans in a higher education setting. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. • Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. • Demonstrate a commitment to providing outstanding customer service skills. • Demonstrate an understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • This position follows a hybrid work structure where in-person is for three to four days and remote for one to two days based on the needs of the office. There will be occasional periods when in person work will be required five days a week based on the needs of the office. • Working from the office is required when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. • This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. • Moves equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $55,322 - $61,146. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 23rd, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Leona Lopez, leona.lopez@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41026&lang=en": {
      "title": "Development Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Admin Assistant II Working Title: Development Assistant FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $50,381 - $55,684 Position #00001851 – Requisition #41026 Join the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Office of Advancement connects those who are passionate about education and research to the people and programs at CU Denver who can excel with their support. We serve as a trusted campus and community resource that inspires alumni pride and private support to advance CU Denver's mission, and we work to ensure a bright and promising future for CU Denver through robust engagement, transformative philanthropy, and a deep sense of pride in the university. The Development Assistant will perform administrative duties and tasks, reflecting substantial variety and complexity, in the Office of Advancement. *This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029. The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days notice of the termination of the term of employment in writing by the University. Development Assistant What you will do: • Provides general office support including but not limited to catering orders, organization of office and donor events, purchasing donor flowers/gifts, printing support, receipts, reservations, and facilitating guest parking. • Performs research and updates, fund and EID look-up support in Salesforce (CU Ascend) for Advancement staff. • Serves as a data and records management resource as it relates to Advancement – understanding the data platforms, information stored and appropriate tools to access requested information. • Serves as primary point of contact and day to day operations for gift handling, accepting donations, creating accurate records and ensuring timely delivery to the Gift Processing unit at the CU Foundation. • Provides backup front desk coverage and presence to greet, direct, and address questions and concerns of visitors in person, as well as via phone and email. • Manages general triage for the Advancement and DA Support email accounts, sorting and distributing mail, scheduling conference rooms, and facilitating meeting setup. • Acts as liaison between the CU Foundation, CU System, and CU Denver campus partners regarding questions, research information, reports, and operations. • Supports team with event bios and briefings for personal meetings, prospect lists, and analyses as needed. • Supports certain events as assigned including but not limited to mailing, packaging, event assembly, prep, and take down. • Maintains cleanliness and orderliness of communal office space including lobby and kitchen; keeps inventory on office supplies, external communication documents, and swag. • Other duties as assigned Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Two (2) years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position Substitution: A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Experience with data management and/or data research. • Experience with Microsoft Excel and CRM database. • Professional experience working in non-profit, events, and/or development/fundraising. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Outstanding customer service skills. • Proficiency and familiarity with Advance, Salesforce, or similar databases. • Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. • Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. • Ability to utilize internet navigation and research tools (e.g., online, printed, etc.) • Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. • Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. • Ability to conceptualize and utilize data. • Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. • Ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously, adapt to changing priorities, manage time and meet deadlines. • Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and internet navigation tools with proven knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet software, email, and internet access software. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required for Advancement events. • This position requires an in-office presence (3 days a week) but does provide flexibility with a hybrid accommodation for remote work at the discretion of the unit. • Requires valid driver’s license. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $50,381 - $55,684. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 23rd, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Nickolas Chabot-Olson, Nickolas.Chabot-Olson@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39037&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SEHD DEAN Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development Working Title: Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development FTE: part-time Salary Range: $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. Position #00626465 Requisition #39037 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The School of Education & Human Development at the University of Colorado Denver is a statewide and national leader for educational quality, access and equity across the education lifespan, from birth through higher education. Members of the school community have been informing policy and practice while addressing the most important challenges faced by individuals, schools, and communities for more than 50 years. We prepare inclusive educational, community, family, and mental health practitioners, scholars, and leaders dedicated to championing change that leads to well-being, opportunity, and life-long learning in the diverse urban, rural, and global communities that we serve. Our Inclusive Excellence Plan reflects our efforts to ensure that those we serve have access to an excellent education through inclusive practice and scholarship in a climate that is responsive to their needs. The school’s degree programs engage students in a strategic and interrelated combination of course work and internships in schools, agencies, and community-based organizations. The school offers three doctoral level programs, an educational specialist degree, 13 master's degrees in multiple program areas, and two undergraduate degrees, along with many licenses, endorsements and certificates. The undergraduate and graduate programs prepare and inspire education and mental health leaders to have a profound impact on fostering opportunity achievement, and success across rural, urban, and diverse communities. Programs are designed to be highly impactful for working professionals and distance learners with evening, online and hybrid class options. Community-engaged and global partnerships are the heartbeat of SEHD. Innovative initiatives co-constructed with school districts, community colleges, and service organizations draw upon personnel strengths in education, human well-being, and equity-centered and community-focused research. These partnerships foster and celebrate diverse community voices, relevant student learning opportunities that build careers, positive outcomes for partner institutions, and outstanding research publications cited around the world. In 2024, SEHD was recognized as the number one graduate online education program in Colorado and among the top graduate education programs in the nation according to U.S. News and World Report. The School of Education & Human Development's strategic plan outlines its commitment to academic excellence, inclusive practices, and community engagement. It emphasizes fostering innovation in teaching, research, and service to meet the evolving needs of students and society. To read the full statement, click here: https://education.ucdenver.edu/about-us/strategic-plan Lecturer The purpose of this posting is to expand our pool of Lecturers available to teach courses for the School of Education & Human Development. Lecturers selected from this pool will become vital members of the School’s innovative education programs. For information on the specific programs and courses offered, please visit https://education.ucdenver.edu. The School of Education & Human Development will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for future appointments to temporary, part-time, non-tenure-track positions. Lecturers are generally limited to two courses per term. This will be a semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. You are welcome to reapply to the new posting at the beginning of each year. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term, the required number of student enrollments in your tentatively scheduled course(s), and budget availability. Thus, we cannot guarantee that you will teach particular courses or that you will actually teach in a given term. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Significant successful teaching or work experience in education, community, or business contexts, especially in urban and diverse settings. • At a minimum, an earned master’s degree in relevant content area (some courses may require a minimum of an earned doctoral degree). See minimum qualifications for each academic level below. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Undergraduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications • M.A. or M.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, or • B.A. or B.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, AND a M.A. or M.S. in any field in addition to at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Education or a closely related discipline, or • If the Master’s Degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must have a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Graduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications MA Degree Programs • PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. • If the terminal degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV Candidates need to supply some evidence of experience (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise). • If the candidate does not have a terminal degree, the candidate must have a M.A. or M.S. AND a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., teaching experience, school principal, board certified counselor, etc.) of experience PhD, EdD, PsyD Degree Programs • PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. • If the doctorate degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate at least 18 graduate level credit hours in related discipline and/or 5 years’ experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Education or a closely related field. • Experience teaching at the graduate level. • Experience teaching online or with blended/hybrid models (e.g. Blackboard or eCollege and LiveText) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Experience with culturally, linguistically, and economically diverse communities, knowledge of urban educational community issues, and an interest in collaborating with a variety of constituencies in an urban environment. • Proficient with basic technology (e.g. MS Office) Conditions of Employment This position involves working closely with students where the person may become aware of campus safety issues that may need to be reported as part of CU’s commitment to compliance with the Clery Act. The person in this role will receive the related training and be required to submit data once per year to the campus Clery Act team. For more information about our commitment to campus safety as it relates to this law, please visit https://www.ucdenver.edu/emergencymanagement/clery-act CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). • Additional materials can be added here if applicable. Questions should be directed to SEHD HR, sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40928&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar for Operations",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCSEOC-Rg Rcrd/Regstr Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Associate Director Working Title: Associate Registrar for Operations FTE: Full Time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $91,766 - $95,000 Position #00679137 – Requisition #40928 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado, Denver | Anschutz Medical Campus CU Denver and the CU Anschutz Medical Campus serve as vital pillars of the University of Colorado system. Located in the heart of the city, CU Denver helps make education work for all by offering unique opportunities at a premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs, across seven schools and colleges. Just a few miles away in Aurora, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus is a nationally recognized academic medical campus, home to six health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked hospitals—UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children’s Hospital Colorado—which together see more than 2.6 million patient visits annually. While on separate campuses, the two universities collaborate in key areas to provide comprehensive support for students, faculty, and staff. The results are powerful: Together, CU Denver and CU Anschutz Medical Campus have earned an R1 classification for conducting cutting-edge and life-changing research that creates impact in our communities. Additionally, for more than a decade, they have received a national Military Friendly® School designation. For more information visit, ucdenver.edu and cuanschutz.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Associate Registrar for Operations position leads and supervises a team of six professionals in the Registrar’s Office who support the academic mission of the university through managing, protecting, and authenticating student records. The team managed by the Associate Registrar for systems is charged with supporting the Registrar operations through systems access and development, document creation and management, curriculum maintenance, catalog production, and course scheduling, and reports to the University Registrar. Associate Registrar for Operations: What you will do: Provide leadership in the Registrars office for Registrar operations Lead the Registrar operations that are conducted through PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, student system development, testing, troubleshooting, and error resolution Support the provision of security access to CU student data systems and applications Manage theproduction services functions to support Registrar office operations Ensure effective us of OnBase imaging, forms, and workflow Oversee the registrar processes for uAchieve degree audit and transfer, Transferology and TES Lead the catalog and curriculum management through the utilization ofLeepfrog CAT and CIM modules, Manage the processes related to the Parchment transcript system software Oversee the processes related to the Paradigm ordering system application Lead the team and processes that utilize the EMS class scheduling software for class and National Student Clearinghouse and National Student Loan Data System enrollment reporting, and related services that include, but are not limited to: Research, policy development and compliance, problem solving, project management, business process design, and infrastructure decision-making. Employee management, including hiring, onboarding, training, development, and performance management. Other Duties as assigned Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor's degree in a related field. Four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in management level positions, including supervisory experience. Experience with systems and applications such as Campus Solutions, uAchieve, Leepfrog, OnBase, Parchment, Paradigm, and EMS. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in computer science, computer programming, information technology, information systems, student affairs, student personnel services, higher education, or related field of study Experience at the Assistant Registrar level or above in a higher education Registrar’s Office. Experience in software development, configuration, and/or regression testing Experience with National Student Clearinghouse and National Student Loan Data System enrollment reporting and reconciliation, Experience establishing, reviewing, and communicating policy, and Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, including successfully communicating technical details to non-technical colleagues. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Strong organizational skills and the ability to handle multiple initiatives simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to generate and implement direction for the assigned area and ensure alignment with the department, divisional unit, and university strategic goals. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. Moves equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. The University of Colorado - Denver is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $91,766 - $95,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation.Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Sep 9, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Meredith Husk, Meredith.Husk@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39036&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SEHD CPE Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) Working Title: Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. Position #00007000 Requisition #39036 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The School of Education & Human Development at the University of Colorado Denver is a statewide and national leader for educational quality, access and equity across the education lifespan, from birth through higher education. Members of the school community have been informing policy and practice while addressing the most important challenges faced by individuals, schools, and communities for more than 50 years. We prepare inclusive educational, community, family, and mental health practitioners, scholars, and leaders dedicated to championing change that leads to well-being, opportunity, and life-long learning in the diverse urban, rural, and global communities that we serve. Our Inclusive Excellence Plan reflects our efforts to ensure that those we serve have access to an excellent education through inclusive practice and scholarship in a climate that is responsive to their needs. The school’s degree programs engage students in a strategic and interrelated combination of course work and internships in schools, agencies, and community-based organizations. The school offers three doctoral level programs, an educational specialist degree, 13 master's degrees in multiple program areas, and two undergraduate degrees, along with many licenses, endorsements and certificates. The undergraduate and graduate programs prepare and inspire education and mental health leaders to have a profound impact on fostering opportunity achievement, and success across rural, urban, and diverse communities. Programs are designed to be highly impactful for working professionals and distance learners with evening, online and hybrid class options. Community-engaged and global partnerships are the heartbeat of SEHD. Innovative initiatives co-constructed with school districts, community colleges, and service organizations draw upon personnel strengths in education, human well-being, and equity-centered and community-focused research. These partnerships foster and celebrate diverse community voices, relevant student learning opportunities that build careers, positive outcomes for partner institutions, and outstanding research publications cited around the world. In 2024, SEHD was recognized as the number one graduate online education program in Colorado and among the top graduate education programs in the nation according to U.S. News and World Report. The School of Education & Human Development's strategic plan outlines its commitment to academic excellence, inclusive practices, and community engagement. It emphasizes fostering innovation in teaching, research, and service to meet the evolving needs of students and society. To read the full statement, click here: https://education.ucdenver.edu/about-us/strategic-plan Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) What you will do: Our Office of Continuing and Professional Education (CPE) provides a wide array of courses, an alternative teacher licensure program, certificates, endorsements, workshops and leadership training tailored to meet your professional development needs. The purpose of this posting is to expand our pool of Lecturers available to teach courses for CPE. Lecturers selected from this pool will become vital members of the School’s innovative education programs. For information on the specific programs and courses offered through CPE, please visit https://education.ucdenver.edu/continuing-education. The School of Education & Human Development will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for future appointments to temporary, part-time, non-tenure-track positions in Continuing and Professional Education (CPE). Lecturers are generally limited to two courses per term. This will be a semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term, the required number of student enrollments in your tentatively scheduled course(s), and budget availability. Thus, we cannot guarantee that you will teach particular courses or that you will actually teach in a given term. This position involves working closely with students where the person may become aware of campus safety issues that may need to be reported as part of CU’s commitment to compliance with the Clery Act. The person in this role will receive the related training and be required to submit data once per year to the campus Clery Act team. For more information about our commitment to campus safety as it relates to this law, please visit https://www.ucdenver.edu/emergencymanagement/clery-act Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Significant successful teaching or work experience in education, community, or business contexts, especially in urban and diverse settings. • At a minimum, an earned master’s degree in relevant content area (some courses may require a minimum of an earned doctoral degree). See minimum qualifications for each academic level below. Undergraduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications • M.A. or M.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, or • B.A. or B.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, AND a M.A. or M.S. in any field in addition to at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Education or a closely related discipline, or If the Master’s Degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must have a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Graduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications MA Degree Programs • PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. If the terminal degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV Candidates need to supply some evidence of experience (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise). If the candidate does not have a terminal degree, the candidate must have a M.A. or M.S. AND a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., teaching experience, school principal, board certified counselor, etc.) of experience PhD, EdD, PsyD Degree Programs • PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. If the doctorate degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate at least 18 graduate level credit hours in related discipline and/or 5 years’ experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Education or a closely related field. • Experience teaching at the graduate level. • Experience teaching online or with blended/hybrid models (e.g. Blackboard or eCollege and LiveText. • Experience with culturally, linguistically, and economically diverse communities, knowledge of urban educational community issues, and an interest in collaborating with a variety of constituencies in an urban environment. • Proficient with basic technology (e.g. MS Office) CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. As of January 1, 2021, Lecturer positions will accrue sick leave at a rate of 0.034 hours per hour worked with a maximum accrual of 48 hours per fiscal year (July 1 – June 30). This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to SEHD HR, sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39022&lang=en": {
      "title": "CU Succeed, Lecturer (Gold)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Aug 21, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-CU Succeed Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Adjunct Lecturer Working Title: CU Succeed Lecturer (Gold) FTE: Part Time Salary Range : non-compensated (see below for details) Position #00722892 – Requisition #20282 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Succeed program seeks currently employed High School teachers as part-time Lecturers. This program enables high school juniors and seniors to take CU Denver courses in their high schools for dual credit during the school day. All applicants into this position are seeking approval as CU Denver Adjunct Faculty members to teach CU Denver courses in the high school where they are already employed. This adjunct lecturer role is a non‑compensated appointment within the CU Succeed program. Individuals approved for this position serve on a voluntary basis and do not receive salary, stipend, or benefits from the University of Colorado Denver. The role is designed to formally recognize and authorize qualified high‑school educators to deliver CU Denver course content in their home schools, in alignment with academic standards and departmental expectations. Participation as an unpaid adjunct reflects a collaborative partnership between CU Denver and Colorado high schools to expand dual‑credit learning opportunities and does not create an employment relationship or guarantee future compensated teaching assignments with the university. CU Succeed Lecturer (Gold) What you will do: Instructors will teach courses in Colorado High Schools. These instructors are approved by academic departments to offer course content for designated courses. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters Degree or 18 credit hours at the graduate level in the discipline you are seeking approval. Currently employed in a Colorado High School. Conditions of Employment This position requires an onsite presence, on the teacher's home high school campus, at the discretion of the home school’s schedule. This adjunct lecturer appointment is a voluntary, non‑compensated role and does not constitute a paid employment relationship with the University of Colorado Denver. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. The position requires the ability to effectively collaborate across functions with both CU Denver faculty and staff and with personnel at the partnering high school, including sustained communication, coordination, and shared academic planning. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits This adjunct lecturer appointment is a voluntary, non‑compensated role and does not constitute a paid employment relationship with the University of Colorado Denver. All compensation and benefits should be handled by the instructor’s home institution. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date, or [DATE]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Current Curriculum Vita, including Education (degrees, dates, institutions attended, etc.), Teaching Experience, Publications and References (names, titles and phone numbers) Undergraduate and graduate transcripts Department specific required education qualifications and additional requirements found here: https://clas.ucdenver.edu/cusucceed/new-lecturer-application Questions should be directed to Leslie Cummings, leslie.cummings@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=35883&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Posted Date: Aug 13, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Chemistry Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/ Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: part-time Salary Range: $1 , 615 p e r credit hour (lower division), $1645 per credit hour (upper division), or $1808 per credit hour (graduate level) Position #00 007315 ID: 35883 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state’s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Lecturer What you will do: The teaching load for this lecturer position is a maximum of two Chemistry or Biochemistry courses per semester . The lecturer will teach the assigned course (s) , hold office hours , and submit grades at the end of each semester accordingly. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. M S in Chemistry or Biochemistry or a closely related field is required D emonstrated record of excellence in teaching. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. Strong commitment to student education and success. Experience in online or hybrid delivery . Physical Requirements the ability to stand and walk for extended periods, bend and reach to assist students, lift and carry moderate weight (like books or supplies), Good vision and hearing, Clear speech, manual dexterity for writing and using technology. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established at $ 1, 615 – 1808, per credit hour accordingly . The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix . Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified , and interviews begin. P reference will be given to complete applications received by May 31, 2025 at 11:59:00 PM . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position . Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate) , and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed t o Laura Cuellar , LAURA.CUELLAR@UCDENVER.EDU. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu ​ ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40606&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Jul 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS - Interdisciplinary Studi Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). Position #00630439 – Requisition #40606 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Interdisciplinary Studies Related courses in designated fields of the discipline, which may include specializations in areas such as Health Humanities, Humanities, Religious Studies, Social Justice, Sustainability, Women and Gender Studies, or another interdisciplinary studies related field for the Interdisciplinary Studies Program in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The Department of Political Science will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Lecturer What you will do: • Teach up to two courses per semester on an as needed basis. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Master’s degree or PhD in Interdisciplinary Studies or related field Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Previous teaching experience • PhD or ABD in Interdisciplinary Studies or related field Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. • Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. • Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. • Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. • Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. • Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. • Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. • Strong commitment to student education and success. • Experience in online or hybrid delivery. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on number of credit hours and whether it is graduate or undergraduate. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Interdisciplinary Studies Related courses. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The department will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40601&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Jul 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SPA - OTHER Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-Time Salary Range: $5,124.01 per 3-credit hour course for Fall 2026. Beginning January 2027, SPA will apply annual merit pool increases consistent with campus guidelines. This position is part of an ongoing pooled posting; rates may differ for Senior Lecturers who are retired or Emeritus SPA faculty. To inquire about the current rate for any appointment type, please contact SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu. Position #00825852– Requisition #40601 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Campus seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track Lecturer positions for the School of Public Affairs. Candidates hired from this pool may teach undergraduate courses in the Bachelor of Public Administration (BAPA) or Bachelor of Criminal Justice (BACJ) programs, or graduate level courses in the school's Master of Public Administration program (MPA), the Master of Public Policy (MPP) program, or Master of Criminal Justice (MCJ) program. If selected, this would be a part-time, semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. This pool will remain active until May 31, 2027, at which point all applicants will be cleared from the pool. Applicants are encouraged to apply to future recruitment pools after that date. US News & World Report places CU Denver's School of Public Affairs as a whole at number 25 nationally, tied with Duke University, Georgetown University and several other prominent institutions. Four of SPA’s academic focus areas—now offered as graduate certificates—are ranked among the top 25 programs nationally. - 10th in environmental policy and management - 13th in nonprofit management - 22nd in public management & leadership - 25th in public policy management Degrees offered include the Ph.D. in Public Affairs, the Master of Public Administration, the Master of Public Policy, the Master of Criminal Justice, the Bachelor of Arts in Criminal Justice, and the Bachelor of Arts in Public Administration. Please visit https:// publicaffairs.ucdenver.edu/ for further details. Lecturer What you will do: Lecturers in the School of Public Affairs (SPA) contribute to the teaching mission across the School’s undergraduate and graduate programs in public administration, public policy, and criminal justice. Teaching assignments may include in-person, hybrid, or online formats depending on program need and instructor expertise. Lecturers may teach no more than two courses per semester or term across all CU campuses. If you are teaching in any unit outside SPA, please make sure to note that in your application. As a lecturer, you will: • Teach one or two courses per term that align with SPA’s curriculum and learning outcomes. • Develop and deliver high-quality, inclusive instruction that reflects SPA’s mission to Lead. Solve. Change. • Foster an engaging, equitable learning environment for a diverse student population of working professionals, traditional students, and community partners. • Design course content and assessments consistent with SPA’s learning outcomes and assessment philosophy emphasizing applied, evidence-based learning and equity-minded reflection. • Communicate regularly with students and provide timely, constructive feedback consistent with SPA’s teaching guidelines. • Collaborate with program faculty and the program manager in the syllabus collection and review process, ensuring syllabi reflect current objectives and university policies. • Participate in instructor communication and onboarding processes and maintain compliance with required training and campus policies. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Candidates must have completed a terminal degree. For most courses, this requires an MPA, MCJ, or Ph.D. in public administration, public policy, criminal justice, or a related field. Candidates must also show strong accomplishment in teaching. • For undergraduate courses: the instructor should possess a relevant graduate degree at least one level above the course taught; if the instructor’s graduate degree is in a non-relevant field, the instructor must have completed at least 18 hours in a graduate program in a relevant field • For master’s level courses: the instructor should possess a terminal degree relevant to the discipline and a record of research, scholarship, or achievement appropriate to the program • For doctoral courses: the instructor should possess a terminal degree relevant to the discipline and a record of scholarship and preparation to teach at the doctoral level • For dual credit courses (e.g., CU Succeed): the instructor should possess the same qualifications as required for undergraduate courses Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Teaching experience in higher education, particularly with adult learners or hybrid/online delivery. • Demonstrated professional experience in public service, nonprofit management, policy analysis, or the criminal justice system. • Experience using Canvas or comparable learning management systems and applying inclusive, high-impact teaching practices. • Evidence of commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in teaching or professional work. • Ability to connect academic theory with real-world application in public affairs practice. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of public administration, public policy, or criminal justice frameworks and their contemporary applications. • Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple course demands. • Cultural competency and awareness of the role of equity and justice in public service education. • Facility with applied learning techniques such as case studies, simulations, community-based projects, and data-driven assignments. • Ability to engage students through accessible course design and learner-centered pedagogy. • Proficiency with online systems as used in course coordination. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • Ability to sustain periods of focused work and communication in online or in-person instructional settings. • Capacity to adapt to varying class modalities (in-person, hybrid, online). • Regular use of computer and learning technology systems. • Commitment to maintaining a respectful, collaborative, and inclusive environment consistent with SPA and CU Denver values. • Occasional evening or weekend work may be required depending on course schedules. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,124.01 per 3-credit hour course for Fall 2026. Beginning January 2027, SPA will apply annual merit pool increases consistent with campus guidelines. This position is part of an ongoing pooled posting; rates may differ for Senior Lecturers who are retired or Emeritus SPA faculty. To inquire about the current rate for any appointment type, please contact SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu.The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This is a pooled posting. Applications are reviewed by each Program Director quarterly. If a vacant teaching need is identified, applicants that fit the qualifications and experience for a particular course may be contacted. Please direct questions to SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu. Thank you! Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. A letter of application which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications 2. A current Resume/CV 3. Proof of degree (unofficial transcript or diploma is acceptable) 4. The names, addresses, daytime telephone numbers and e-mail addresses for 3-5 professional references, either attached to your resume/CV or uploaded as a separate document 5. Lecturers may teach no more than two courses per semester or term across all CU campuses. If you are teaching in any unit outside SPA, please make sure to note that in your application. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Please do not submit any of your application material (via email) to the job posting contact. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40482&lang=en": {
      "title": "CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/18/2026 Posted Date: Jul 21, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-CU Succeed Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver) FTE: Part Time | In-Person Salary Range : $4,002 per 3 credit course Position #00723102 – Requisition #40482 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Succeed program enables high school juniors and seniors to take CU Denver courses in their high schools for dual credit during the school day. All applicants into this position are seeking approval as CU Denver Adjunct Faculty members to teach CU Denver courses that are requested by Denver area High Schools. The posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for the CU Succeed Silver program. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of Denver area High Schools. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. This temporary Lecturer recruitment pool is anticipated to remain continuously active. CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver) What you will do: Instructors will teach courses in High Schools. These instructors are approved by academic departments to offer course content for designated courses. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters Degree the discipline you are seeking approval, or a Masters Degree with at least or 18 credit hours at the graduate level in the discipline. Ability to travel to locations requiring a lecturer CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range for this position has been established at $4,002 per 3 credit course, per semester. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date July 21st, 2026. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Current resume or Curriculum Vita, including Education (degrees, dates, institutions attended, etc.), Teaching Experience, Publications and References (names, titles and phone numbers). Undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Department specific required education qualifications and additional requirements found here: https://clas.ucdenver.edu/cusucceed/new-lecturer-applicationDepartment specific required. Questions should be directed to Leslie Cummings, leslie.cummings@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40420&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Jul 7, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Music & Entertainment Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate) FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range: $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position # 00726509 – Requisition #40420 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) Department features some of the best contemporary-focused music industry programs in the country. With about 500 students, MEIS has one of the biggest music business, recording arts, singer/songwriter, and contemporary performance programs in the Western U.S. Our downtown Denver location is perfect for enabling our students to be very involved with the thriving Denver music scene while they are in the program. As one of the only music departments in the country with a contemporary focus, Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) at CU Denver provides students with the guidance, knowledge, and expertise needed to transform passion for music into a lifelong profession. This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of 6 months. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate) What you will do: 100% Teaching You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) As a Lecturer in Recording Arts (Undergraduate), your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next generation of contemporary musicians. This can include instruction in the following: • Basics of Audio Production • Advanced Audio Production • Mixing Techniques • Mastering Techniques • Critical Listening • Pro-Tools Lab • Digital Audio Workstation Techniques and application • Live sound Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BA/BS/BM in Music or a related field Or substitution of tested experience as exemplified by one or more of the following: • Engineering, mixing, or mastering a recording(s) with a reputable label • Extensive experience as a reputable studio or live sound engineer • Evidence of mixing/engineering sound for a national/international tour/festival • Evidence of recording published/performed by a major artist/publishing/media outlet (i.e. film or TV show) or company • Two years successful experience teaching at a major university or college in same or similar program Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Master’s Degree in Music or a related field • Experience teaching Music at the college level Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. • Ability to balance multiple projects and tasks while maintaining attention to detail. • Ability to create equitable and positive experiences for all. • Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. • Demonstrate influential ability to embrace and advance equity and equitable inclusion. • Ability to establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. • Strong judgment and critical thinking skills. • Ability to authentically listen and communicate relevant information, anticipate problems, and offer suggestions for resolution. • Demonstrate dedication to mentoring students to best realize their potential as artists in society. • Demonstrated excellence and experience in organizational teamwork, communication, and interpersonal skills CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of 6 months. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications 2. Current CV or résumé Questions should be directed to Evan Shelton, evan.shelton@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40266&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Landscape Architecture",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Jun 18, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAP-Landscape Arch Dept Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Landscape Architecture FTE: .225 per 3-credit course or .45 per 6-credit course Part-time Salary Range: The salary for this position as been established at $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course or $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course Position #00642344 – Requisition #40266 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting establishes a pool of candidates who can teach one studio or technical seminar per semester in Landscape Architecture on an as needed basis. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. Single course appointments will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through August 2026, at which point, all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer What you will do: The Department of Landscape Architecture in the College of Architecture and Planning at the University of Colorado Denver is seeking a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments will be made. Lecturers selected from this pool will teach in the College’s graduate program. Classes taught may range from three to six credit hours and may include lectures, seminars, and studios in all teaching modes (in-person, hybrid, online, remote). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A master’s degree in Landscape Architecture or a related field, or a terminal degree and expertise in the course content is required. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Preference may be given to applicants with prior teaching experience, a record of professional practice in landscape architecture, and a professional degree in a related field. Applicants for courses addressing specific subjects are also given consideration based on the course needs; in this case, they must have an advanced degree or proven expertise in the topic. Applicants should have substantive knowledge of the landscape architecture field and/or the subject matter which they will be teaching.Individuals with multidisciplinary education and expertise are strongly encouraged to apply. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, across various modalities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills that support building positive, respectful relationships with students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff in a collegial academic environment. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Ability to adapt teaching strategies to different course formats (in-person, online, hybrid) and student needs. Ability to foster an inclusive classroom environment that encourages respectful dialogue across diverse perspectives. Ability to incorporate inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support student success. A commitment to inclusive excellence, including supporting students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Conditions of Employment The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary for this position has been established at: $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course. $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This part-time appointment is not eligible for group health, life insurance, or retirement benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months - Dec 31, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to CAP Human Resources, CAP.HR@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
