    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39736&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Electrical Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5825.00 per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per 1-credit lab. Position #00619467 – Requisition #39736 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate level courses as needed in the Department of Electrical Engineering on a part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term. This position is paid on a per-course basis. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments and are paid on a per course basis. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: • Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. • Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. • Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. • Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. • Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • A Master of Science degree in electrical engineering or in a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. • A PhD degree in electrical engineering or related fields is required for teaching graduate level courses. • A Bachelor of Science degree in Engineering or a related field is required to teach undergraduate labs. Substitution: • A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. • A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. • Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. • Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. • Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. • Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. • Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. • Most courses require presence on campus at least twice a week. • The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. • This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. • The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5825.00 per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per 1-credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline • Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Mark Golkowski, mark.golkowski@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39735&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Dean of Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5825.00 - $6500 per 3-credit course Position #00782785 – Requisition #39735 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver, College of Engineering, Design and Computing, seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate level courses as needed in the following departments: • College of Engineering, Design and Computing Dean’s Office. • Department of Biomedical Engineering. • Department of Civil Engineering and Construction. • Department of Mechanical Engineering. Positions are part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term and may include required courses, technical electives or labs. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments and are paid on a per course basis. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: • Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. • Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. • Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. • Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. • Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • A Master of Science in Engineering or a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. A combination of a Bachelor’s degree. • A PhD in Engineering or a related field is required for teaching graduate level courses. • A Bachelor of Science degree in Engineering or a related field is required to teach undergraduate labs. Substitution: • A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. • A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. • Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. • A professional engineering license is preferred. • Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. • Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. • Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. • Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment • Occasional work during the evening may be required. • Most courses require presence on campus at least twice a week. • The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. • This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. • The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5825.00 - $6500.00 per semester per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per semester per 1-credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline • Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • List of Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Amy.Fauver@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39732&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Computer SC & Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $6500 - $7500 per 3 credit course; $3250 per 1 credit lab. Position #00605249 – Requisition #39732 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate or graduate level course(s) as needed in the Computer Science and Engineering Department on a part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term. This position is paid on a per-course basis. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments. The department is interested in experienced software engineering professionals to teach undergraduate security courses, undergraduate level discrete structures and graduate level software engineering courses. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: • Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. • Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. • Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. • Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. • Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • A Master of Science degree in computer science or a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. • A PhD degree in computer science or related fields is required for teaching graduate level courses. A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. • Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. • Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. • Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. • Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. • Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment • This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. • Occasional work during the evening may be required. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. • The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $6500 - $7500 per 3 credit course; $3250 per 1 credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This is an open continuous position for AY26/27. Once you apply you will be placed on our candidate inventory list and will continuously be considered for positions as vacancies become available. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Kelly Konrad at Kelly.p.konrad@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39309&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Director, CFDA",
      "description": "Posted Date: Mar 16, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Associate Director Working Title: Associate Director CFDA FTE: Part-time (0.5 FTE) Salary: $10,000 stipend plus course buy-outs Position #00781410 – Requisition #39309 About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state’s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development & Advancement (CFDA) is seeking a visionary Associate Director (AD) who is passionate about empowering faculty and shaping the future of academic life at CU Denver. This is an exciting opportunity for a campus leader who thrives on building community, designing innovative development experiences, and helping colleagues unleash their full potential. In this role, you will directly influence the faculty experience—strengthening pathways for growth, fostering belonging, and creating the kind of campus environment where faculty excel, connect, and thrive. Working closely with the Director, the AD will co-create impactful initiatives for faculty across the Denver campus. Key areas of focus include developing tailored mentorship programs, building professional learning—especially for IRC faculty—and supporting the Center’s core programming. This position may also lead interactive workshops (virtual and in person), host topic-based faculty communities, assist faculty with career and dossier development, and engage in a wide range of activities that foster growth, belonging, and excellence. In partnership with the Director, the AD will lead, design, and deliver programs that support faculty of all ranks and disciplines. Associate Director, CFDA What you will do: • Collaborating with the Director to plan strategic programming, services, and initiatives, with particular attention to IRC faculty’s career advancement and professional development needs. • Designing and facilitating mentorship programs (individual, peer, group) for faculty at all ranks as well as developing programs to support mentors for inclusive and effective mentoring practices. • Supporting faculty as they prepare for rank advancement. • Engaging across campus to elevate CFDA’s visibility and strengthen partnerships. • Leading innovative efforts to strengthen community, belonging, and engagement among faculty. • Work with the Director to manage the CFDA grant programs. • Identifying opportunities for improved practices and implementing solutions that strengthen departmental and campus-wide faculty development. • Assessing faculty needs using research-informed data collection methods. • Working with faculty groups and academic leaders to design tailored professional development programs for faculty. • Consulting with faculty on professional, scholarly, and career development goals. • Performing additional duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. • Current rostered University of Colorado Denver faculty member. • Terminal degree in any discipline from an accredited institution. • At least three (3) years of rostered faculty experience at CU Denver. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) • Experience designing and delivering professional learning opportunities. • Expertise in evidence-based and innovative approaches to faculty development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to build strong, collaborative relationships across all campus levels. • Strong knowledge of CU Denver faculty policies and practices. • Excellent collaboration, communication, and facilitation skills. • Strategic, innovative thinker responsive to faculty needs. • Demonstrated commitment to campus engagement, equity, and inclusion. • Knowledge of best practices in faculty mentoring and development. • Strong understanding of promotion and/or tenure processes. • Leadership experience and the ability to launch new initiatives and solve problems creatively and efficiently. • Demonstrated mentoring skills and enthusiasm for supporting others’ growth. • Ability to write, present, lead discussions, and provide one-on-one consultations effectively. • Ability to incorporate faculty well-being and community-building principles into programs. • Strong organization skills, with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects independently and collaboratively. Conditions of Employment • This 9-month role is approximately a 0.5 FTE appointment. Faculty will continue their duties within their program area at 0.5 FTE. The appointment will begin in August 2026 running through May 2027. The expected term is three (3) years, each year renewal will be based on successful performance of the job duties in the pervious year. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements • The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The position will include a $10,000 stipend and expected to approximate a .5 FTE. For faculty with a teaching load of 5 courses or less per year, there are 2 course buyouts per academic year, for faculty with a teaching load of more than 5 courses per year, there are 3 course buyouts per academic year. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline • Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by April 6, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). • Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Bryn Harris, Director of the CFDA, bryn.harris@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38598&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Jan 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Mathematics Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title : Lecturer FTE: Part Time Salary Range: The hiring rate (or budgeted rate) for this position has been established at $1,667 per credit hour (undergraduate level) or $1,808 per credit hour (graduate level). Position # 00763623 – Requisition # 38598 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Department of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences is housed on the Auraria campus in the heart of Denver's commercial, cultural, and recreational district. Its location in downtown Denver attracts a diverse population, comprising both traditional and non-traditional students. This diversity is enriched by our commitment to a philosophy of inclusion, embedded in all aspects of campus life from its community members, curriculum, research and community service, allowing for the creation of a learning environment that welcomes, embraces, sustains and celebrates the unique and shared experiences of faculty, staff, and students. This posting is a pool for continuous faculty hires. The Department of Mathematical & Statistical Sciences has an opening for a temporary, non-tenure track, part-time lecturer to teach mathematics and statistics courses. The appointment is for one semester, with the possibility of renewal for future semesters. Lecturer What you will do: Design and Deliver courses. Deliver lectures, seminars, and tutorials. Design and deliver assessments, such as exams, assignments, and reports. Collaborating with other lecturers, faculty and course coordinators to improve teaching methods and expand knowledge base. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree A Master’s degree in mathematical sciences from an accredited university; OR A master’s degree in any area and 18 credit hours of graduate-level course work in mathematical sciences. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) A record of successful teaching at the secondary or college level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate Effectively, both in Writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with other department employees. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to teach a diverse student body. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Commitment to applying rules in a consistent manner Ability to present in a classroom in an engaging way. Ability to work effectively with students on a 1-to-1 basis. Ability to provide clear feedback on student written work. Flexibility and empathy in adapting to student circumstances. Conditions of Employment Most courses offered by the department are delivered in person, and the successful candidate will be required to teach on campus. While there may be occasional opportunities to teach hybrid or online courses, these are dependent on departmental course availability and scheduling needs. Remote or hybrid teaching is not guaranteed and will be determined by the assigned course mode. Candidates should be prepared for a primarily in-person teaching role. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The hiring rate (or budgeted rate) for this position has been established at $1,667 per credit hour (undergraduate level) or $1,808 per credit hour (graduate level).The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Review of applications will begin in early 2026 and this position will remain open until filled for the 2026 - 2027 semester / academic year. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Statement of teaching philosophy Unofficial transcript(s) Questions should be directed to Stephen Hartke, Stephen.Hartke@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41358&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Production Support Professional",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/22/2026 Posted Date: Oct 15, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: University InformationServices Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: University Information Systems (UIS) provides technical services and enterprise applications to the University of Colorado campuses and the Office of the President. UIS is committed to excellence in customer service and technical expertise. Through the development of enterprise applications, UIS supports the University as a whole with systems used by students, faculty, human resources employees, finance employees, and others. The Sr Production Support Professional assists in the management and oversight of all batch processing for the University of Colorado systems and applications. This position serves as a technical professional with the ability to understand IT processes, troubleshoot, test, create technical documentation, and assist university stakeholders with any inquiries that the team may receive. This position will provide support to Production Support Professionals through issue resolution. This position is heavily involved in scripting and automation to meet sophisticated customer requirements more efficiently. The Sr Production Support Professional will need to have a solid basis of IT knowledge and the ability to work on an on-call schedule. This position is Essential Services. Positions falling into Essential Services are required to work their normal hours even when the office is closed during a normal or holiday week. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Production Services and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Serve as a technical professional to support production batch processing: resolve daily issues, build new processes, file transfers, monitoring processing, data security, and maintaining all aspects of a production environment. Remove manual tasks by building automated processes using scripting to solve complex customer requirements. Ensure high-availability and stability of production environments. Troubleshoot sophisticated, tier-2 technical production issues. Resolve higher level issues and provide expert support to Production Support Professionals. Escalate issues as needed to Principal Production Support Professional. Work independently and directly as a team member with other Production support and other IT departments. Work closely with development teams to support their work efforts. Develop thorough documentation for systems, processes, and procedures. Follow change control processes. Enhance existing and create new processes and procedures by replacing manual tasks with automation Participate in an on-call rotation and shift work as necessary. Provide excellent customer service to internal and external customers while developing positive customer relationships. Creation and testing of automated batch processes. Migrations for all Enterprise Systems. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $68,150. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) Three (3) years’ equivalent experience in a service desk, call center, data processing center or other customer service environment Preferred Qualifications: Five (5) years’ equivalent experience in production services, including: Batch experience UNIX or Linux administration Documentation for systems and processes/procedures Understanding of change control processes Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: Knowledge of data processing and batch production processes Ability to design, develop, and troubleshoot complex scripts to meet specific customer requirements and automate repetitive tasks efficiently. Proficient in Linux-based servers, ensuring high availability and security. Proficient in writing complex cURL commands to interact with APIs, web services, and perform data transfers securely and efficiently. Ability to configure email scripts for efficient and reliable job scheduling and automation working with prompt sets, call objects, rule definitions, and spreadsheet parsing. Knowledge of IT policies and standard methodologies Demonstrated self-starting initiative with the ability to work with minimal guidance Ability to work independently and directly as a team member with other Production support and other IT departments. Ability to work a flexible schedule – including off hours, weekend, and holiday on-call hours Ability to prioritize work tasks and projects while meeting deadlines Ability to deliver a high level of commitment to customer service Able to articulate clearly via email and phone conversations Attention to detail Basic computer skills such as Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Microsoft Teams, etc.) Excellent troubleshooting and problem-solving skills How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by October 22, 2026 . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41355&lang=en": {
      "title": "Customer Experience Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 15, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Procurement Service Center Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: Do you enjoy building relationships with diverse audiences, continuously learning, and being the go-to person for your customers? If so, this position is perfect for you. This role is a part of the Procurement Service Center (PSC), which is responsible for the purchasing, payables, contracts, commercial card, strategic sourcing, sustainability, small business program, and travel for the University of Colorado’s (CU) four campuses and the Office of the President. As a Customer Experience Specialist, you will provide training and support to customers needing assistance with Procurement Service Center (PSC) functions. You will be an expert in guiding customers on the use of PSC tools such as PeopleSoft, Concur, CU Marketplace, and others as they arise. Additionally, you will promote employee compliance by interpreting University policies related to procurement, commercial cards, travel, purchasing, and accounts payable. You will also constantly seek ways to improve the customer experience by offering insights into resource and training development to help customers succeed in managing PSC processes. This role is crucial to the PSC’s mission of delivering excellent customer service. This position reports to the Customer Success Program Manager and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff System. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible for a hybrid schedule, working some days from home and some days in the office at 1800 Grant St, Denver, CO. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Support and Service: Provides individualized training and support to employees and affiliates across all four campuses and the Office of the President on the use of various complex tools, including the Concur Travel & Expense system and CU’s Marketplace e-procurement system through email, phone, video meetings, virtual office hours, and webinar training. Responds to a high volume of email and phone interactions, simultaneously throughout the day during the PSC’s core operational hours of 8 a.m.-12 p.m. and 1 p.m.-5 p.m. MST. Remains up to date on PSC and University policies and provides guidance to partners and customers on their applicability Assists external suppliers by researching the status of payments, identifying resolutions for payment delay, and assisting in the supplier request and registration process Instructs internal and external customers on Procurement Service Center website resources, including navigating to policies, procedures, forms, learning resources, tax and other information Investigates issues, identifying when action is required by other resources, and escalating to appropriate stakeholders as necessary Utilize procurement tools (Concur, CU Marketplace, PeopleSoft Finance, etc.) as needed to complete basic system tasks and provide easy resolutions for campus customers Takes quick action on escalating potential issues with systems or policy when short-term customer contact trends suggest the need Interacts regularly with PSC personnel to learn and stay current on business processes, policies, and tool configuration Identifies gaps in content and creates content to support knowledge and AI chatbot functionality. Work on special projects as assigned. Knowledge Collection and Process Improvement: Self-starter that continually looks for opportunities to increase knowledge in internal PSC functions to better support customers. Develops relationships and builds trust with customers as the front line into the PSC Provides professional, accurate and timely resolution to customer inquiries Tracks and manages contacts, tasks, research, and communications using CRM and other specialized tools/software Creates content for the PSC Knowledge Base in the form of Knowledge Articles that can be utilized to accurately resolve future inquiries as it relates to PSC processes and policies. Work on special projects as assigned. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $56,500-$60,000. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) One (1) year of professional work experience in a customer service role (e.g., inbound help desk/call center; or other customer engagement environment) Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of professional work experience in a customer service role supporting a business, procurement, finance, and/or educational function Experience with one or more of the following: General procurement practices Procure to pay business processes eProcurement and financial systems Salesforce Service Cloud Peoplesoft Chatbots Managing customer inquiries through Live Chat functionality Professional experience working in a higher education institution Experience using Artificial Intelligence (AI)-driven solutions in support of customers and business operations Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: Impeccable customer service skills Oral, written, listening, and interpersonal skills (including the ability to facilitate interaction, communication, and teamwork between others), along with excellent comprehension skills A teaching mindset and skillset, including the ability to utilize multiple methods with one individual in order to ensure learning is received and retained Collaboration skills, including the ability to work (in-person and remotely) with others from different areas and backgrounds to reach a common goal Computer skills, including proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, along with the ability to research and implement new software/tools to advance office goals and business processes Organizational skills, with the ability to work under pressure, manage multiple concurrent/competing projects, and adapt to changing priorities while maintaining personal effectiveness and strong customer service Critical thinking skills, including the ability to identify problems, questions, and assumptions; establish significance; and develop new ideas and initiatives that improve the performance of the organization Customer service skills, including the ability to actively listen, address customer needs, defuse tense situations, and maintain an open, flexible, and friendly demeanor Ability to work independently in a highly dynamic, flexible, and fast-paced environment Ability to learn technical, policy, and procedural information quickly and to retain it well Ability to utilize AI solutions to assist or perform business operations Knowledge of AI ethics and data privacy considerations in the workplace Knowledge of natural language prompting (NLP) Ability to produce content, ideate, edit, and perform analysis How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by Tuesday, October 20th . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41419&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/12/2027 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Ethnic Studies Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE : part-time Salary Range: The hiring rate for this position has been established at $1,704 per credit hour for undergraduate courses per semester or $1,849 per credit hour per graduate courses per semester. Position #00653636– Requisition #41419 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Lecturer What you will do: This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching general Ethnic Studies courses, such as the Introduction to Ethnic Studies, Indigenous Studies and courses within their area of expertise, for the Department of Ethnic Studies in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. Lecturers may be asked to teach on campus or fully online. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. We will contact you if an opening suits your qualifications. The Downtown campus is located in the heart of the city's commercial, cultural and recreational district. Its location in downtown Denver attracts a diverse population, comprising both traditional and non-traditional students. This diversity is enriched by our commitment to a philosophy of inclusion, embedded in all aspects of campus life from its community members, curriculum, research and community service, allowing for the creation of a learning environment that welcomes, embraces, sustains and celebrates the unique and shared experiences of faculty, staff, and students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master's degree in Ethnic Studies or related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience teaching Ethnic Studies courses. Experience teaching online using the Canvas LMS. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The hiring rate for this position has been established at $1,704 per credit hour for undergraduate courses per semester or $1,849 per credit hour per graduate courses per semester. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [October 14, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Edelina Burciaga, Edelina.Burciaga@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41345&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SPA - OTHER Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Assistant Professor Working Title: Assistant Professor – Criminal Justice FTE: Full-Time Salary Range: $76,000 - $87,000 Position #00008187– Requisition #41345 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit cudenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The nationally-ranked, NASPAA accredited School of Public Affairs (SPA) at the University of Colorado Denver seeks a full-time 9-month/academic year Assistant Professor for the CJ programs within SPA, starting fall of 2027. The standard teaching load is four courses over the academic year in person and online (2 in each semester). There may be additional summer teaching opportunities available as a separate contract as well. The candidate must be able to teach in our BACJ and MCJ cores, as well as some elective courses within the CJ programs. A strong research trajectory is required. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and sustain an active program of high-quality research, including actively pursuing external funding. Experience with externally funded research, including participation in or leadership of grant proposals, is highly desirable. We are seeking a very collegial scholar, who feels comfortable doing CJ research/teaching within a broader applied social science/public affairs school setting. Experience working with scholars from other related fields is a plus. Assistant Professor – Criminal Justice What you will do: Teaching: Teach courses online and in-person as needed by SPA Teach courses at both the Undergraduate and Graduate (master’s) level as needed by SPA May teach cross-listed courses with Public Administration, and Public Policy programs as needed by SPA Areas of expertise and teaching areas that we are looking for could include, but are not limited to: Criminological Theory, Interpersonal or Community Violence, Courts, Victimology, Statistics and Research Methods, Data Visualization, GIS, Mixed Method Design, and Practice-Informed Analysis. Service & Leadership Contribute to the ongoing growth of the Criminal Justice program through committee service, student mentorship (formal academic advising provided by professional advisors in the School), serving as a second reader on capstone projects, and positively contributing to SPA programs Research To help us achieve our campus goal to become internationally known for our research and creative work, the successful candidate will be expected to develop and sustain a strong program of high-quality research and contribute to the overall research agenda of the School of Public Affairs. Expectations include producing peer-reviewed scholarship and actively pursuing external funding. Interest and experience in collaborative and interdisciplinary research are desirable. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. PhD in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Public Administration, Public Policy, Political Science, Public Affairs, Sociology, or a closely related field. Applicants must have teaching experience and effectiveness in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Public Affairs/Public Policy, and/or Sociology programs. A strong research trajectory. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Demonstrated ability/experience teaching online classes Success and/or experience with grant funded research Experience designing and teaching courses with a university learning management system (preferably Canvas) Ability and experience teaching at the graduate and undergraduate level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Willingness to contribute to the holistic growth of the Criminal Justice Program Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding student service skills and a student-centered attitude Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. The search committee may conduct a limited number of preliminary interviews during the ASC Annual Meeting. These interviews may be scheduled through and conducted in the ASC Employment Exchange designated interview area. Participation in conference-based interviews is optional and will not adversely affect consideration for this position. Applicants who are not attending the conference will have alternative interview opportunities available. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is eligible now and in the future for visa sponsorship. While the hiring unit is willing to pursue visa sponsorship, an offer of employment will be contingent on the candidate having a visa status that allows employment with the University as of the start date for the position or the University’s petition being approved and on the candidate being able to obtain the appropriate visa status. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $76,000 - $87,000 per academic year depending on experience and other qualifications. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Monday, November 9, 2026 a 11:59:00 PM. . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant teaching experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and specifying any experience or abilities that you meet in our preferred qualifications list. The letter should speak to your ability and/or experience teaching students across different modalities (in-person, online, hybrid, etc). Curriculum vitae / Resume List of three to five professional references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Any FCQs or student evaluations for the last 2 years, if available. Questions should be directed to: Chris Smith at chris.smith@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41374&lang=en": {
      "title": "Creative Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/13/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: LIB LIBRARY Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Intermediate Professional Working Title: Creative Technology Specialist FTE: Full time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $58031 - $64140 Position #00716247 – Requisition #41374 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Creative Technology Specialist will support the work of the Innovation Garage and Digital Media Studio, two of the Auraria Library’s dynamic service points. This position works directly with students, faculty, and staff of the Auraria Campus across a variety of areas including graphic design, large format printing, 3D printing, and related makerspace tools, photo and video cameras, and audio equipment. This position provides consulting services in professional resources and tools related to these areas. As one of the primary service providers for the Innovation Garage and Digital Media Studio, the Creative Technology Specialist oversees daily operations, ensuring the consistent application of policies and procedures, supporting the work of Access and User Services colleagues, staff, and student employees. Creative Technology Specialist What you will do: I nnovation Garage Duties Provides expert consulting services in large format printing, vinyl cutting, 3D printing, image digitization, maker tools and other creative technologies. Monitoring email inquiries, booking calendars, assisting users, and maintaining equipment. Maintains a safe and comfortable environment for creative technology service users, thus creating a positive user experience. Provides users with tools and services to bring their ideas to life. Works across the Library to promote understanding and use of Creative Technology Services. Provides formal and informal technology training to library staff and campus faculty, staff, and students. Performs inventory, monitoring, and ordering supplies as needed. Stays current with creative and maker trends through continuing education, research, and environmental scans. Evaluates creative hardware and software and makes upgrade recommendations as part of continual service improvement. Documents and refines workflows and other standard operating procedures. Employs problem-solving and critical thinking skills to arrive at creative solutions to complex issues. Ensures Innovation Garage website content is up to date. Collects, analyzes, and applies data to inform decision-making. Provide recommendations for equipment purchases and repairs. Contributes to a positive working environment. Digital Media Studio Duties Maintains extensive knowledge of and ability to operate DMS photography, video, and audio equipment and related software. Monitoring email inquiries, booking calendar, assisting users, and maintaining equipment. Fulfills appointments by setting up equipment properly and on time, assisting users, maintaining equipment, and creating a positive user experience. Ensures Digital Media Studio website content is up to date. Assists in training other staff on DMS operations and equipment use as needed. Provides informed recommendations for equipment purchases and repairs. Incorporates critical research into DMS practices and services. Additional duties Member of Library committees and task forces as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor's degree in related discipline, such as digital design or film production. 1+ years of professional experience in digital media, educational/creative technology, or related fields. Customer service experience. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience supervising a service point supporting student success in a higher education setting. Experience creating and maintaining workflow documentation. Experience in a library or higher education environment. Supervisory experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Advanced proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud or related products. Advanced knowledge of and experience working with image and video projects. Advanced knowledge of a variety of makerspace services and equipment. Inventory monitoring experience. Ability to solve technology problems quickly and creatively. Effective learning and presentation skills. Ability to work independently and in team settings. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Experience with Microsoft Office products including Excel, Word, and Outlook. Conditions of Employment Work Hours: Monday-Friday; 8:00am – 5:00pm. Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position is primarily in person to support users, equipment, and daily operations, with limited hybrid work available based on the needs of the library. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $58,031 - $64,140. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 13, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications. A current CV/resume. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Peyton Hertz, at PEYTON.HERTZ@UCDENVER.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41538&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior DevOps Engineer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/04/2026 Posted Date: Oct 28, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: University InformationServices Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: University Information Services (UIS) provides technical services and enterprise applications to the University of Colorado campuses and the Office of the President. UIS is committed to excellence in customer service and technical expertise. Through the development of enterprise applications, UIS supports the University systems used by students, faculty, human resources employees, finance employees, and others. The Senior DevOps Engineer applies an automation mindset leveraging DevOps tools with the application of technical skills and leadership to the areas of application and infrastructure deployment, patching, and support. This position will serve as a senior technical expert within the UIS Enterprise Cloud Services group. As a part of the ECS CrossApps Middleware team, the Sr. DevOps Engineer performs installation, configuration, upgrade, and day-to-day operational support of a variety of applications and middleware technologies. This position designs, builds, and maintains technical environments, supports system rollouts, responds to and troubleshoots escalated operational issues while managing internal and external customer relationships. This position informs and advises project managers and stakeholders about project plans and implementation, conducts technical analysis, and produces recommendations. This position is also charged with supporting daily operations of these applications, and must also work with the team to automate processes and procedures, create efficiencies, and provide quality business services to our clients and customers. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Enterprise Cloud Services and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Serve as a senior technical architect and systems integrator for large complex systems and applications, including monitoring, orchestration, and automation. Communicate and collaborate with application owners/managers, initiative leaders, and project leadership to clarify requirements, develop work plans, document, and lead technical architecture. Apply DevOps methodologies for building and operating highly available, scalable applications and services. Evaluate, build and modify automation for deploying applications and services based on DevOps and GitOps principles internally and for external teams Serve as a domain architect providing advice and guidance on new technical solutions and/or architectural changes to existing design, particularly as it pertains to the CrossApps Middleware areas of discipline and support. Maintain, upgrade, and extend a library of Ansible playbooks, Bash, and Python scripts. Configure applications with GitOps, GitLab deployments, and RESTful APIs. Generate monitoring from Ansible inventory variables and other primary sources. Prevent drift between environments (e.g. DEV, TEST, STAGE, PROD). Enforce operational scalability and availability of applications, patching, and monitoring of applications. Configure applications for stability, security, and maintainability using technologies such as cloud, on premise, containerization, and DevOps principles. Troubleshoot application issues in collaboration with application owners/managers and enterprise infrastructure staff. Debug SSL/TLS Respond to and resolve outages and drive postmortems. Providing direction and mentoring others in a leading contributor role. On-call support and occasional weekend maintenance support. Develop standards for configuration, documentation, and management. Draft process documentation and internal training to the team. Coordinate with infrastructure, identity/access management, integrations, and other service providers in planning and/or executing maintenance windows, evaluating and working toward resolution of impacts on application and authentication portfolio. Provide backend support for Oracle Fusion Middleware products and various unique applications. Create and maintain base container environments. Apply patches and upgrade applications. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $110,000. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelors’ degree from an accredited institution of higher education or equivalent professional experience. (The educational requirement may be substituted by professional experience on a year-for-year basis). Five (5) years’ experience with a combination of the following: Application engineering and automation technologies, based on enterprise architecture standards. Designing, implementing, and supporting, enterprise-ready container orchestration platforms. Developing and supporting CI/CD pipelines. Experience leveraging industry standards building services in IaaS/PaaS/Cloud environments. Reading and writing code in multiple languages. Linux systems administration Oracle Fusion Middleware: Java application servers; WebLogic; Oracle Identity Solutions (e.g., OUD, OID, OVD, OIM), and/or Ping Identity; Oracle Service Bus; Oracle Enterprise Data Quality, Oracle SOA Suite Experience working with Tableau, Cognos, Neo4J Experience working with Docker, Rancher 2 and Kubernetes Configuration management and scripting Preferred Qualifications: Seven (7) years’ experience with a combination of the following: Certifications and/or demonstrated experience in major cloud platforms (i.e. AWS, GCP, Azure, Oracle Cloud), container orchestration platforms (i.e. K8), and configuration management tools (i.e. Ansible). Demonstrated experience configuring and utilizing monitoring, alerting and logging solutions, such as Elastic Stack (aka ELK Stack) and Greylog Experience implementing or integrating with standards-based Identity and Service Providers (e.g., OpenID Connect, SAML2) Experience constructing highly secure, reliable, and performant solutions with open-source technologies. Experience working in a 24x7 operational environment with on-call and production support responsibility. Experience with disaster recovery planning and testing Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: Be a self-starter, quick learner, curious investigator, and a programmer (shell scripting). Solid knowledge of networking, Linux (and some Windows) system administration, web servers, application servers, database servers, SSL/TLS, logging, clustering, monitoring, RESTful APIs, and container/orchestration. Ability to apply best practices, design patterns, and DevOps / GitOps principles. Envision automating everything such that all the organization’s systems could be re-created from a git repo. Ability to troubleshoot, resolve, and explain complex problems and discuss trade-offs of potential solutions. Skilled in finding, fixing, repairing, and preventing issues. Ability to learn and use new applications and computer languages, including the use of source control Ability to work in a twenty-four-seven (24x7) operational environment with on-call and production support responsibilities Ability to work remotely while remaining attentive, engaged, responsive, and productive Knowledgeable in supporting Enterprise Java applications. Strong attention to detail. Excellent oral and written communication skills. How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by November 4, 2026 . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41539&lang=en": {
      "title": "Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Senior Professional Working Title: Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid | Term – Limited Salary Range: $63,000 - $65,846 Position #00853744– Requisition #41539 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * *This is a term limited position that is currently funded for 1.5 Years (18 Months).* The position will be reviewed after 18 months of employment to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days’ notice of the term of employment in writing by the University. About GSO The newly reconstituted Graduate Studies Office (GSO) supports graduate students, faculty, and programs at CU Denver by defining and maintaining campus wide graduate policies and procedures; coordinating administration of graduate assistantships and tuition remission; overseeing academic progress and degree completion; and advancing enrollment, retention, and student engagement initiatives. The Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator is a faculty- and staff-focused position that provides leadership and support for all academic administration activities of the Graduate Studies Office at the University of Colorado Denver. Job functions include tasks like coordinating with graduate program directors, graduate council, registrar, and admissions to develop and maintain transparent and campus-consistent catalog access to campus-consistent policies and procedures for all graduate certificates, licensures, and degrees; coordinating with academic affairs, HR, and faculty affairs to ensure faculty and program compliance with campus-level accreditation expectations; coordination with program directors, registrar, and admissions to provide comprehensive and consistent process for documents and records related to student admissions and progress; coordinating student training in pedagogy; coordinating faculty training in student mentoring; other activities that directly support the academic mission of the Graduate Studies Office. Supervision of student employees may be required. Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator What you will do: Graduate Program Information and Accreditation Compliance Partner with academic affairs to ensure campus (HLC) accreditation compliance for all certificates, licenses, and (D1, D2, D3) degree programs. Partner with program directors, admissions, and registrar to scaffold catalog templates for communicating certificate and program information in the graduate academic catalog. Maintain GSO website to provide transparent, comprehensive and consistent access to admissions and graduation requirements for all (D1, D2, D3) degree programs. Graduate Student Academic Records Partner with program directors, registrar, and admissions to improve campus-consistent systems for routing academic forms that are maintained in the student applications and record management systems Manage emails related to graduate student records and appeals submitted to the graduateeducation@ucdenver.edu inbox Graduate Faculty Appointment Records Partner with graduate council, faculty affairs, HR, institutional research and effectiveness to develop and maintain updates and campus-wide access to the annotated list of graduate faculty members. Manage website, documents, and schedule for graduate council. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university, or 4 years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position. Two (2) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Four (4) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Master’s or terminal degree from an accredited college or university. Experience with university website, catalog, admissions, and student records software. Familiarity with accreditation requirements for graduate programs. Familiarity with diversity of graduate program types. Experience coordinating cross-disciplinary teams in higher education settings. Prior experience working in the Graduate Studies Office or Graduate School at CU Denver. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels across the university. Ability to perform duties independently without guidance and direction from other professionals. Ability to manage multiple projects and tasks that require high attention to detail. Ability to manage day-to-day workflow, administration, and oversight of project processes. Conditions of Employment This is a term-limited position that is currently funded for 18 months Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $63,000 – 65,846. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 10, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Mike Wunder, michael.wunder@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41457&lang=en": {
      "title": "HRIS Functional Analyst Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Employee Services Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: The University of Colorado System Administration, which also houses the Office of the President, is located in the uptown neighborhood of Denver with a few smaller offices located on the campuses. Many of our departments support the educational and research missions of the four University of Colorado campuses, but System Administration is not considered a campus. We provide diverse opportunities for professional development, innovation, and collaboration with talented staff and faculty. The Employee Services (ES) department provides the CU community with excellent services from recruitment to retirement. This office provides technical expertise while administering benefits, payroll, individual tax management, and strategic HR programs. The functional areas of ES include Payroll, Technologies, Benefits, Retirement, Learning and Development, International Tax, and Human Resources. The HRIS Program Manager requires a strong, experienced HRIS/HCM professional with enterprise systems experience and expertise in Core HR, Payroll, Benefits, Time and Absence Management, and HR/GL, as well as a strong HR background, including knowledge of HR policies and procedures. This position will represent Employee Services as an HCM expert and act as a liaison to our campus partners, internal department units, and University Information Services teams. The position takes ownership of assigned HCM/HRIS processes, enhancements, and initiatives across the entire HCM platform. The position leads and contributes to HCM/HRIS projects and operational initiatives from initial intake and requirements gathering through solution development, testing, implementation, communication, and post-implementation tasks. This position requires strong cross-functional knowledge of the PeopleSoft HCM application, solid understanding of processes and setup, experience with system integrations, and an understanding of HR and payroll rules. This role will actively consult and partner with Campus HR offices, University Information Services teams, and the Employee Services department to guide process improvement, support new initiatives, and drive best practices and strategic change across the university. The position will interact closely with ES team members and campus business partners to understand system configuration requirements and to achieve and maintain accurate system data. The position will ensure that system configurations align with institutional and legislative requirements and will work with the appropriate system subject matter experts when changes need to be recommended. The position will play a key role on the ES HRIS team in providing project support, system testing, end user support, day-to-day operational support, documentation, and training. The ability to extract and analyze data to identify trends, analyze and document system functionality, and provide support to the team and system users are key components of the position. The ideal candidate for this role can benefit from having a background in or knowledge of higher education. This position is customer oriented and dedicated to providing solutions to increase efficiency and compliance, maximize use of HCM features and functionality, and optimize the user and customer experience. This position reports to the HRIS Assistant Director and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff System. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: HRIS Program Ownership and Functional Leadership Serve as a subject matter expert functional lead and provide oversight for PeopleSoft HCM across all modules including Core HR, Payroll, Benefits, Time and Absence Management, and HR/GL Lead HCM projects that support HR initiatives through the entire project life cycle including requirements discovery and documentation, solution design, testing, and implementation Apply in-depth knowledge of HCM system features and functionality to provide solutions that meet the complex needs of individual departments, campuses, and the cross-campus community Understand and account for cross-module dependencies in solution designs, testing, and implementations Effectively manage and document integrations between HCM and other HR-related systems System Operations and Compliance Develop new or enhance existing business processes to create efficiencies and ensure compliance Build strategic partnerships and collaboration with internal teams to identify and document areas for improvement for data quality and process efficiency and effectiveness Build audit tools using SQL and PS Query to identify gaps, overlaps, and contradictions within data sets or configurations and identify potential root causes. Lead comprehensive efforts to address issues and resolve root causes Work with ES HRIS team to identify policy-related, process-related, or procedural problems that lead to system and/or data inconsistencies. Recommend changes to ensure compliance with HR policies and data quality standards Perform day-to-day and cyclical operational tasks owned by the ES HRIS team including performing various mass updates using excel-to-Cis, application engines, and other mass-update processes Stay abreast of university, state, federal, and other regulatory requirements and ensure system configurations and operational tasks remain current and in compliance Relationship Management, Training, and Support Develop and maintain relationships and continuous communications with UIS, the HR campus community, and other campus HCM and HR technology stakeholders Apply knowledge of CU business processes, product and functional best practices, applicable federal and state laws and university policy, and related technology trends to guide stakeholders toward appropriate HR technology solutions Facilitate educational opportunities and cross-campus collaboration between campus HR colleagues regarding HCM functionality and enhancements, including system best practices and business process change Develop materials for user training and education and partner with other subject matter experts on user support materials including procedure guides, system definitions, calendars, and other documentation related to HRIS Assist with keeping documentation and process guides updated. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $112,000-$116,000 . CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) Five (5) years’ experience that includes one or more of the following: Experience working in a functional analyst (FA) or business analyst (BA) capacity or similar; which may include at least (2) years of experience working with PeopleSoft HCM as an FA or BA and experience writing SQL queries Experience with data extraction and analysis Experience with system and end user testing, including issue analysis, documentation, and resolution Preferred Qualifications: Seven (7) years of equivalent experience as stated above. One (1) year of experience in a team lead or supervisory role, which may include assigning and reviewing the work of others, providing guidance to internal and external team members, and/or assisting management with performance reviews (this requirement may be substituted by formal leadership training) Experience and a knowledge of relational databases, particularly PeopleSoft HCM HR, Payroll, and Benefits tables Experience creating and diagnosing queries using PS Query or SQL writing applications Experience in higher education HR information systems and/or payroll systems Experience with project coordination or project management Experience as a business or functional analyst that includes some of the following components: Documenting business processes. Understanding system requirements, business cases, and functional specifications. Writing test plans. Analyzing and troubleshooting software application issues. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position, employees will need to know the following: Knowledge and experience with performing data extraction and analysis Experience with systems such as: Human capital management systems Ticketing management systems Project management systems Experience identifying problems, proposing solutions and a willingness to take ownership through to resolution or ensure a clear hand-off. Demonstrated ability to work independently and to balance multiple concurrent tasks and responsibilities with changing priorities while maintaining personal effectiveness Ability to switch from sophisticated to routine tasks when required. Strong analytical and design skills Demonstrated knowledge of relational databases Ability to interpret and evaluate user requirements and analyze business systems. Abllity to work with partners with varying levels of technical experience. Demonstrated success completing cross functional projects Energy and initiative in solving problems. Adaptable and willing to undertake a variety of tasks. Strong written and oral communication skills. Ability to communicate with individuals from a diverse set of backgrounds. How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by Sunday, November 1st. Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41542&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Marketing",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Marketing FTE: Part-time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00853110– Requisition #41542 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Marketing from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Marketing What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Marketing classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Marketing or other related degrees. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least eight years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in closely related course topic. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41534&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/18/2026 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Student Success & Transitions Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Executive Director Working Title: Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement FTE : Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: 105,000 – 115,000 Position #00679912– Requisition #41534 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement (STFE) provides leadership, direction, and long-term planning for programs that support students through key transitions and foster early engagement in the university experience. The portfolio includes New Student Orientation and Family Engagement, First-Year Experiences, and Peer Advocate Leaders. The Executive Director collaborates with colleagues and student leaders in STFE to ensure alignment with unit, divisional, and institutional priorities that support a coordinated, student-centered approach to student success. This role also serves as a key collaborator within the Division of Strategic Enrollment and Student Success (SESS), continually evaluating and implementing innovative approaches to support student success across in-person, hybrid, and remote environments. Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement: What you will do: Provide leadership and development for professional staff and student employees, including onboarding, performance management and evaluation, training, team building, and workplace wellness. Provide oversight and strategic management to the following programs: New Student Orientation and Family Engagement, including orientation experiences for first-year and transfer students and their families, extended orientation, enrollment efforts, and innovative onboarding and reengagement initiatives. First-Year Experience programs, including course offerings through First-Year Seminar and College Success (UNIV 1110), and faculty recruitment, training, and development. Peer Advocate Leader (PAL) program, including innovative peer mentoring for new undergraduates, and opportunities for student development. Lynx Summer Academy (i.e., summer bridge) for first-year students, including program planning, recruitment, course selection, program evaluation, and funding acquisition. Foster cross-campus collaboration and partnerships with academic departments, student support offices, faculty, staff, and other university stakeholders to coordinate services, identify emerging student needs, and develop integrated approaches to student engagement, persistence, and success. Establish and advance continuous improvement efforts across assigned programs and services, using best practices, student feedback, and relevant data to evaluate effectiveness, strengthen student outcomes, and align initiatives with university and Student Success goals. Provide reports to leadership on orientation and registration of new students, FYE persistence and retention, and Lynx Summer Academy persistence and retention. Streamline and continually improve communications with students and families by coordinating with Admissions and University Communications to ensure that all outreach to students are timely, specific, and targeted. Oversight of all program budgets and work with Directors to ensure resources allocated for each fiscal year are effectively deployed and processed in alignment with institutional procedures and policies. Participate in committee work with SESS and academic affairs colleagues to improve access, streamlined transitions, and student success and development. Represent CU Denver and STFE at events and programs on and off-campus. Serve on campus committees, working groups, and/or task forces related to Student Success initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree from an accredited institution in related field. Seven (7) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in a higher education setting leading student enrollment, retention, graduation efforts, and/or other related higher education experience. Five (5) years of experience in a supervisory or administrative position in higher education or similar field (i.e., education, business or non-profit). Experience managing budgets. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Earned doctorate in educational leadership or higher education or related field from an accredited institution. Experience in a comprehensive urban university. Experience with traditional age, older, and diverse student populations. Evidence of effective creation and execution of programs that are best-practice informed models. Experience with grant administration, pre- and/or post-award. Experience working with EAB Navigate360. Demonstrated experience leading a team of diverse faculty, staff, and community members. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to lead a team of diverse faculty, staff, and community members. Demonstrated evidence of the ability to effectively devise and manage budgets. Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence and student success. Leadership experience and skills in conceiving and carrying forward new initiatives. Skills in identifying problems, analyzing data, and making recommendations. Ability to be creative, innovative, and willing to take risks to accomplish the goals of the institution. Strong interpersonal skills. Consensus builder with the ability to bring about constructive change using participatory processes. Excellent organizational and coordinating skills. Skilled in communicating effectively in writing, public presentations, and individual or group consultations. A demonstrated ability to integrate principles of equity and inclusion into programs and practices. Ability to work in partnership with faculty, administrators, staff, and students from across the university. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to successfully prioritize among multiple tasks and manage multiple project on distinct timelines. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position generally requires an onsite presence on campus; however, employees may be allowed to work remotely up to one day per week. The ability to work remotely will be determined by the supervisor. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $105,000 – $115,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 17, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Erika Larson, erika.larson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41508&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Management",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Management FTE: Part-time, less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00715302 – Requisition #41508 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The CU Denver Business School Management program seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Management What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Management classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Management or closely related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. Depending on course modality, this position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials : To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that upon hire, applicants will be asked to provide original transcript(s) of their highest degree and two (2) letters of recommendation. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41507&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in International Business",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in International Business FTE: Part-time, less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00756279 – Requisition #41507 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in International Business position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in International Business What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach in the International Business discipline at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, remote or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in International Business, MBA, International Studies, or closely related field. a closely related field to the course topic. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in International Business, International Business Negotiations, International Trade, International Management, International Marketing, E-Commerce (including Cross-Border E-Commerce), Global Supply Chain Management, International Finance, and related areas. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in international business and related discipline. Ability to teach online courses (asynchronous and synchronous) Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for overtime, nor benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials : To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of reference upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41505&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Information Systems",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Information Systems FTE: Part-time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00695889 – Requisition #41505 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Information Systems What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Information Systems classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include preparing and delivering rigorous instruction aligned with curricular objectives and learning outcomes, supporting students from diverse backgrounds, assessing student learning, and adhering to program and university policies. Teaching may span areas such as AI and agentic systems, enterprise systems and platforms, cybersecurity, data and analytics, cloud and digital technologies, and other contemporary and emerging areas of Information Systems. Classes may be offered at the undergraduate or graduate level and delivered in person, online, or in hybrid formats. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Information Systems or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior teaching experience in Information Systems or a closely related discipline. Teaching or professional expertise in one or more contemporary and emerging I.S areas, such as AI and agentic systems, enterprise systems and platforms, cybersecurity, data and analytics, cloud technologies, or other emerging technologies. Ability to connect technical concepts and emerging technologies with managerial, strategic, and organizational application. Experience incorporating current industry practices and applied learning into the classroom. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in Information Systems or a related discipline. Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching, mentoring, and student learning. Ability to translate disciplinary knowledge and industry practices into effective classroom learning. Commitment to inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support students from diverse backgrounds. Effective written and oral communication skills. Ability to plan, develop, and deliver courses aligned with established learning objectives and program expectations. Ability to work collaboratively and maintain effective relationships with faculty, staff, students, and other university stakeholders. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [ Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41504&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Entrepreneurship FTE : Part-Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: Minimum $6,000+ depending on total course enrollment at census date Position # 00790682 – Requisition #41504 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The Jake Jabs Center for Entrepreneurship at the CU Denver Business School seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Entrepreneurship and Innovation, from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through January 2027, at which point all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer in Entrepreneurship What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Entrepreneurship classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in a closely related field to the course topic. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least three years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in higher education. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at a minimum of $6,000 per three-credit course; the rate may be increased depending on total course enrollment at census date. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Clair Seville, Jake Jabs Center for Entrepreneurship Assistant Director of Operations, at clair.seville@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41501&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Finance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Finance FTE: Part Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | In- Person Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00683765 – Requisition #41501 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Finance from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Finance What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Finance classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Finance or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least two years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) PhD in Finance or closely related field. Prior online teaching experience in Finance and the record of teaching multiple finance courses. Professional designations such as CFA AND CFP are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026].. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that upon hire, applicants will be asked to provide original transcript(s) of their highest degree and two (2) letters of recommendation. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41500&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Business Analytics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Business Analytics FTE: Part Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00350293 – Requisition #41500 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in Business Analytics position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Business Analytics What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach Business Analytics courses at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Operations Research, Statistics, Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Operations Management, or closely related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in Business Analytics, Statistics, Operations Management, or Operations Research, and the record of teaching multiple analytics-focused courses. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least three years of duties and responsibilities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of recommendation upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41499&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Accounting",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Accounting FTE: Full-time or part-time: Part- Time Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00601531 – Requisition #41499 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in Accounting position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2025-2026 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Accounting What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach in the Accounting discipline at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, remote or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master's degree or terminal degree in Finance, Accounting, Payroll, Fiscal Reporting, Fiscal Management, Financial Forecasting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and additional certifications, licensures, and/or trainings as applicable. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in Accounting. Professional certification/licensure in accounting or allied field, e.g., CPA. CMA, etc. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of reference upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to:Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41496&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance FTE: Part-Time Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per combined undergrad/graduate courses. Position # 00708584 – Requisition #41496 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Risk Management & Insurance from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through January 2027, at which point all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Risk Management & Insurance classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Business, Finance, Risk Management and Insurance, Marketing, or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least 10 years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior teaching experience in Risk Management and Insurance, in-person, online, and hybrid, or at least one of these modalities. Professional designations such as CPCU and ARM are a plus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026,]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
