    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41528&lang=en": {
      "title": "Principal Career Consultant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/09/2026 Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Business School Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title : Academic Services Principal Professional Working Title: Principal Career Consultant FTE: Full Time 1 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $72,028 - $79,610 Position #00802117– Requisition #41528 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This position requires a high level of professionalism, senior leader interactions, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and tact & meeting facilitation. Jobs in this career family provide direct professional support for the teaching and/or educational service mission of the university. Functions include academic advising/counseling, student personnel administration, recruitment and admissions, registration, financial aid, faculty affairs, library services, curriculum administration, and others involving direct support of the educational mission of an academic unit. Principal Career Consultant What you will do: Meet with undergraduate and graduate Business School students and alumni to advise on Resumes, LinkedIn Profiles, Job and Industry Targeting, Networking, Interviewing, and other pertinent career and professional development topics. Ensure students are aware of career opportunities, and employers are receiving quality candidates. Serve as a liaison between students, the university, university services (CU Denver Career Center, Experiential Learning Center, etc.), and Business School Departments (RMI, Jake Jabs Center for Entrepreneurship, Academic Advising, Admissions, J.P. Morgan Center for Commodities, CITI, etc.). Interact with faculty, school clubs, associations, strategic employer partners, and other clients of the Business School to promote connections in the Business School. Through networking and relationship building, strives to connect students and employers for mutually beneficial relationships. Plan, implement, and lead in student and alumni outreach events, which include workshops, career fairs, and job events, information sessions, and other Business School club events. Stay ahead of industry trends, mentor others on the career team, and propel the direction, coaching, and momentum of the team informally Please note, this is not an exhaustive list of responsibilities and roles. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) A bachelor’s degree in a directly related field from an accredited institution. Five (5) years of experience in education, career advising, recruiting, human resources, student support, professional development, or related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualifications Master’s or Terminal Degree in Counseling, Business, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Experience providing career coaching, career advising, or professional development support, including guidance on resumes, LinkedIn profiles, interviewing, networking, and job-search strategies. Experience in recruiting, talent acquisition, human resources, or hiring, with an understanding of employer expectations and hiring practices. Knowledge of business career pathways, industry trends, and internship and full-time recruiting practices. Experience working with students, alumni, and professionals of all career levels (early-career, mid-career, director-level, and executive level) Experience facilitating career-readiness workshops, presentations, or other professional development programming. Experience using career services platforms, applicant tracking systems, and job board sites. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Experience working with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Knowledge of and contacts within the business community and skill utilizing Colorado-based businesses and professional organizations for networking pipelines. Ability to establish and maintain external relationships with businesses and other employers and with graduates of the Business School. Excellent MS Office skills (Outlook TM, Word TM, Excel, PowerPoint TMM), with knowledge of LinkedIn and other social networking applications. Ability to work independently with excellent follow-up and self-starter skills. Well-organized and self-confident, with excellent professional presentation skills. Strong attention to detail in all work products. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure three days in office, two days remote weekly. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position will be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in an in person or remote setting. Remote work requires maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $72,028 - $79,610 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until Nov 9, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Tilda Gross at tilda.gross@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41533&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer – J.P Morgan Center for Commodities & Energy Management",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/24/2027 Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer – J.P. Morgan Center for Commodities & Energy Management FTE: Part-Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Remote Salary Range: $8,000+ (Dependent on enrollment) Position # 00805334 – Requisition #41533 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers* The CU Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The J.P. Morgan Center for Commodities & Energy Management at the CU Denver Business School seeks applicants for a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments are part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will occur as teaching needs arise. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through Jan 2027, at which point all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer – J.P Morgan Center for Commodities & Energy Management What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach classes in their area of expertise with application to Commodities and/or Energy Management related occupations. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at the graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes are expected to instruct remotely but may be asked to instruct in other or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or terminal degree in a business or subject-related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience working in the capacity of a consultant, preferably with an ongoing position that is client facing. Prior experience teaching or guest lecturing in a graduate program on the topic of business. Previous experience collaborating with MBA-level projects, either as a facilitator, participant, or client. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position requires remote work. Lecturers may have opportunities to engage onsite instruction as determined by the modality of evolving and new programming. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $8,000 per 3-credit graduate course and may increase depending on course enrollment at census date. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services.Compensation for non-3-credit appointments will be set at a pro-rated amount and based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to Three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 26, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker, brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41456&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Scientist, PRN",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 26, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: CEDC-Bioengineering ATP Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Research Scientist Working Title : Research Scientist, PRN FTE: Part time | In-Person Salary Range: $30-$50/hour Position #00717646– Requisition #41456 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver is seeking applications for the position of a PRN Research Scientist- Assistive Technology Professional, Clinician, Physical Therapist. UC Denver is the premier research university in Colorado, serving more than 30,000 undergraduate, graduate and health professions students in Denver, Aurora and online and awarding nearly 4,000 degrees each year. The renowned researchers and award-winning faculty of UC Denver offer more than 100 degree programs through 13 colleges and schools. In 2024-25the University was awarded more than $27.5 million in research grants and contracts. The new Anschutz Medical Campus includes over 5 million square feet of research, educational and clinical space on 227 acres. The Downtown Campus is located in one of America's most vibrant urban centers, just steps from the Denver Center for Performing Arts, the LoDo District and the state capitol. On both campuses, students, staff and faculty have access to a broad array of academic, professional, community, recreational and cultural opportunities. Research Scientist, PRN What you will do: All job responsibilities are provided within the Center for Innovative Design and Engineering (CIDE) program, with primary scope of work occurring within CIDE’s specialty outpatient clinic. CIDE’s Assistive Technology Clinic provides one-on-one services to individuals with a disability to improve their overall health and function through the acquisition and use of appropriate assistive technology. Primary responsibility within the clinic program will be in wheelchair seating and mobility, with possible secondary responsibilities such as nighttime positioning and 24-hour postural care and/or worksite accommodation. Additional job responsibilities of this position may include participation in research, teaching and other projects as assigned. Provide Services in our Clinic Program – 100% Support clinic team in the ongoing delivery of state-of-the-art clinical intervention services in complex rehabilitation and assistive technologies. Provide a comprehensive assessment of an individual’s needs to help determine the most appropriate technology, and participate in equipment fittings, adjustments, programming, and training after it is acquired. Work with and communicate effectively with relevant partners in the provision process such as complex rehabilitation technology (CRT) suppliers, manufacturing representatives, and other key stakeholders. Provide required clinic documentation and reports in a timely manner. Provide required documentation on device demonstrations and equipment loans, when required, in a timely manner. Maintain professionalism and responsibility for productivity and quality service delivery. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Licensed Physical Therapist Minimum of 15 years clinical assistive technology experience with complex patients and prescription of complex rehabilitation technology Assistive Technology Professional (ATP) credential Seating and Mobility Specialist (SMS) credential Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Clinical experience with custom contoured seating systems Specialty knowledge in nighttime positioning and 24-hour postural care; Prior experience in research and/or teaching Candidate must have the ability to work independently with excellent communication and organizational skills. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty and staff. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to work effectively as part of a team and independently. Ability to work efficiently and comply with required appointment documentation deadlines. Ability to meet productivity expectations. Ability to work well with diverse populations, commitment to diversity, experience working with cultures other than their own, experience interacting with communities of color. Experience with incorporating diverse perspectives and fostering an inclusive environment. Conditions of Employment This position requires an onsite presence, on campus. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $30.00-50.00 per hour. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the Nov 1, 2026, 12:59:00 AM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Michelle Jaramillo, MICHELLE.JARAMILLO@CUANSCHUTZ.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41485&lang=en": {
      "title": "Temporary Career Counselor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/05/2026 Posted Date: Oct 22, 2026 Job category: Student/Temp Department: AVCSCE-Career Services Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Denver Department: Denver Career Services Job Title: Temporary Career Counselor This is a Temporary position limited to no more than 9-months. Job Summary: This position provides comprehensive career counseling and advising to a diverse body of undergraduate students, graduate students, and alumni regarding goal setting, major/career direction, skill analysis, résumé preparation, job search, networking strategies, and interviewing skills. The part-time career counselor will provide one-on-one advising by meeting with undergraduate and graduate students and alumni through drop-in and scheduled appointments. The part-time career counselor will plan and complete Boots to Suits sessions through May 2027 and complete class/group presentations. Key responsibilities: · Lead career-focused presentations for classes other campus groups · Provide career counseling for students; assess students’ individual needs and direct them to appropriate services as needed · Attend Career Services team meetings remotely · May include supporting on-campus programs such as Boots to Suits Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule of # days per week on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. Why Join Us: The CU Denver Career Center is a collaborative, student-focused office that supports students and alumni in exploring career options, gaining professional experience, and achieving their career goals. We serve a diverse student population across all majors and career stages through individualized career counseling, career education, employer partnerships, and experiential learning opportunities. We seek a part-time Career Counselor who is committed to a student-centered, empathetic approach, providing personalized guidance that empowers students to build confidence and make informed decisions as they navigate their career journeys. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. · A Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, Psychology, Communication, Sociology, Counseling, Liberal Arts, Education, Human Service, Student Affairs, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. · Two (2) years of professional level experience in career counseling, coaching, and/or advising in a higher education setting (internships may be included). Preferred Qualifications: · A Master’s degree in Counseling, Student Affairs, Higher Education or a directly related field · Two (2) years of experience career counseling, coaching, advising, and/or generally supporting culturally and ethnically diverse individual’s development in Higher Education or college setting (excluding internship). · Experience attending and/or facilitating workshops, professional training and/or certificate/licensure in the MBTI, SII, and/or GallupStrengths. · Experience meeting with online students and facilitating virtual programming such as presentations and workshops. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · Strong counseling and natural leadership skills, ability to connect with students and assess their needs. · Exceptional presentation skills and ability to facilitate discussions. · Experienced with Handshake or other career management platform · Outstanding customer service skills. · Proficient with technology such as Microsoft Office 365 and videoconference/webcam (Zoom, Google Hangouts, etc.). · Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. · Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. · Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Joan Fishburn, Joan.Fishburn@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until November 5, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The hiring rate for this position has been established at $28.00 / hour. The above salary rate represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate at the time of posting. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. Temporary employees are only eligible for sick leave benefits. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Denver is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41477&lang=en": {
      "title": "Graduate Contracts and Finance Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/05/2026 Posted Date: Oct 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Senior Professional Working Title: Graduate Contracts and Finance Coordinator FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid | Term – Limited Salary Range : $63,000 - $65,846 Position #00853742 – Requisition #41477 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . *This is a term limited position that is currently funded for 1.5 Years (18 Months).* Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The position will be reviewed after 18 months of employment to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days’ notice of the term of employment in writing by the University. About the GSO The newly reconstituted Graduate Studies Office (GSO) supports graduate students, faculty, and programs at CU Denver by defining and maintaining campus wide graduate policies and procedures; coordinating administration of graduate assistantships and tuition remission; overseeing academic progress and degree completion; and advancing enrollment, retention, and student engagement initiatives. The Graduate Student Contracts and Finance Coordinator is a student- and staff-focused position that provides leadership and support for all financial administration activities of the Graduate Studies Office at the University of Colorado Denver. Job functions include tasks like coordinating with finance and HR offices across campus to develop and maintain campus-consistent, transparent processes for awarding and administering student assistantships and tuition remission; administering dissemination of student fellowship and travel awards; coordinating across the Denver and AMC campuses to assist in developing structural support for student and faculty applications for research and training grants; for student and faculty training in responsible research conduct; for graduate student professional development; and other activities that directly support the research and training missions of the Graduate Studies Office. Supervision of student employees may be required. Graduate Contracts and Finance Coordinator What you will do: Graduate Student Assistantships and Tuition Remission Partner with HR, registrar, and the office of institutional research and effectiveness to develop procedures for centralized review and approval of graduate student assistantships and for determining tuition remission eligibility. Partner with school and college staff to support transition and stabilization for graduate student hiring policies and practices. Partner with local and central finance and the bursar to provide tuition remission for eligible student assistantships. Student Services and Finance Support Manage emails related to graduate student appointments, fellowships, and travel award requests submitted to the graduateeducation@ucdenver.edu inbox. Identify opportunities to improve workflows, documentation, and service delivery. Research and Professional Development Partner with office of research development, office of strategic enrollment and student success, and AMC staff to identify and act on opportunities to improve graduate student and graduate faculty training in research and professional development and in responsible research conduct Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university, or 4 years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position. Two (2) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Four (4) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Master’s or terminal degree from an accredited college or university. Experience with university personnel, financial aid, and finance management software platforms. Familiarity with diversity of graduate research and creative activity programs. Experience coordinating cross-disciplinary teams in higher education settings. Prior experience working in the Graduate Studies Office or Graduate School at CU Denver. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels across the university. Ability to perform duties independently without guidance and direction from other professionals. Ability to manage multiple projects and tasks that require high attention to detail. Ability to manage day-to-day workflow, administration, and oversight of project processes. Conditions of Employment This is a term-limited position that is currently funded for 18 months Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $63,000 - $65,846. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 4, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to: Tyler Keyworth, tyler.keyworth@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41418&lang=en": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor (Open-Rank)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/30/2026 Posted Date: Oct 16, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: CLAS-Advising Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services (Open Rank) Professional Working Title: Academic Advisor (Open Rank) FTE: Full-Time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: (Open Rank - See Below) Position # 00674358 – Requisition #41418 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit www.cudenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences recognizes academic advising is integral to student success. The person in this position will collaborate with a team of academic advisors, faculty, and administrators to support students from entry to graduation. Members of the CLAS Academic Advising team share a strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, student advocacy, and student success. The successful candidate for this position should be prepared to articulate their passion for supporting diverse college students through a developmental and culturally responsive orientation to academic advising. Additionally, the successful candidate should demonstrate their experience working effectively and collaboratively as part of a team to support a high volume of students. Academic Advisor (Open-Rank) What you will do: Academic Advising Engage in developmental and inclusive practices to advise a richly diverse caseload of new and continuing CLAS undergraduate degree-seeking students through to graduation. Advance equity by understanding and advocating on behalf of the needs of all student populations including students of color, first-generation, first-time to college, transfer, veteran, international, and online students. Partner with students to develop advising relationships that foster students’ sense of belonging to college and campus communities. Communicate timely, consistent, and accurate information about degree requirements including general, CU Denver Core, CLAS, and academic program (i.e., major and minor) graduation requirements. Develop a depth of knowledge and understanding of specific major and minor requirements to advise a focused caseload of CLAS majors and minors. Interpret and communicate information about complex college and university policies and procedures. Document detailed notes from email, phone, online/virtual, scheduled and drop-in advising contact with students. Deliver individualized support that is responsive to student needs and facilitates relevant referrals to campus resources. Engage in professional development activities to remain current with academic advising best practices. New Student Programs Prepare for and facilitate in-person and virtual academic advising presentations and appointments for groups of first-time, first-year, and transfer students, including online-only students, during New Student Orientation. Support and implement processes to ensure the accuracy of new student records and Degree Audits related to prior learning credit (e.g., Advanced Placement, International Baccalaureate, Dual or Concurrent Enrollment, and transfer credit). Collaborate with campus partners to promote new student engagement experiences (e.g., First-Year Experiences) that support students through their transition into CU Denver and CLAS. Retention and Graduation Develop, conduct, and track proactive outreach campaigns to advising caseload, including specific student populations, using advising tools and systems. Implement retention and early intervention initiatives for students in need of academic support, including students on different levels of academic standing. Collaborate with campus constituents to promote student engagement experiences (e.g., internships and independent studies) that assist students in exploring and preparing for careers or post-baccalaureate education. Collaborate with campus partners (e.g., Center for Undergraduate Exploration & Advising, Admissions, Registrar, Student Transitions and Family Engagement, First-Year Experiences, etc.) to support campus-wide student success initiatives. Proactively monitor students’ degree progress and support students’ development of academic plans using advising tools and systems. Support returning and readmitted students, including students returning from academic suspension. Complete initial and final graduation checks for fall, spring, and summer graduates. Committee and Campus Involvement Represent CLAS Academic Advising on college and university committees. Serve as a primary academic advising liaison to designated CLAS academic departments, programs, and university student affairs partners. Partner with liaisons in CLAS academic departments to remain current on and communicate major and minor program updates or changes to the CLAS Academic Advising team. Collaborate with the CLAS transfer credit and degree audit team and major advisor(s) to support transfer credit evaluation and degree audit functionality. Advising Systems and Technology Use CU Student Integrated Systems (CU-SIS), uAchieve®, EAB Navigate360, CollegeSource® Systems (i.e., TES and Transferology Lab), OnBase®, and Slate by Technosolutions to advise students. use web-based tools (e.g., Zoom®, Microsoft Teams®, and Qualtrics®) to facilitate academic advising presentations, including online/virtual advising appointments, communicate with colleagues, and support assessment of advising initiatives. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Academic Services Professional A bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university One year of full-time professional-level higher education experience in an academic advising or student affairs office or position Twelve (12) months of paraprofessional experience at the graduate level (e.g., graduate assistantship experience) in an academic advising or student affairs office or position may be counted toward the full-time professional-level experience. Academic Services Senior Professional A bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Three years of full-time professional-level higher education experience in an academic advising or student affairs office or position (paraprofessional experience, including graduate assistantship experience, may not be counted as full-time professional-level experience) Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) One (1) or more years of direct experience working with undergraduate students in academic advising or new student or retention programs, including orientation, early action, student and academic support programs, or other enrollment and retention activities. Demonstrated skills and experience utilizing technology to support proactive and effective academic advising practices and processes across multiple modalities (i.e., in-person, phone, and virtual/remote). Demonstrated success supporting a large and diverse caseload of students. A master’s degree (completed or in progress) in higher education, student affairs, college student personnel, counseling, education or related fields from a regionally accredited college or university or two years of full-time professional-level higher education experience in an academic advising or student affairs office or position. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of higher education systems, college student development, and student success practices. Knowledge of and ability to apply culturally responsive, inclusive, and equity-centered practices in support of providing outstanding academic advising and student service. Skill in building trusting and highly collaborative relationships with individuals from diverse backgrounds, including students, team members, faculty, administrators, and campus partners Skill in communicating complex information clearly and effectively through written, oral, and virtual modalities. Skill in using technology and learning new software systems to manage information, communicate, and support student services. Ability to apply effective listening, critical thinking, sound evaluation, and problem-solving skills to complex situations. Ability to accurately manage, analyze, organize, and document student, academic, and institutional information with attention to detail, accuracy, and quality. Ability to organize and prioritize independent work and multiple responsibilities in a high-volume, fast-paced environment. Ability to contribute to additional role-, team-, and office-connected responsibilities as needed. Conditions of Employment The CLAS Academic Advising Office supports approved flexible schedules and hybrid work consistent with the needs and responsibilities of this position. This position may be responsible for additional relevant activities that support the work and mission of the CLAS Academic Advising Office. Please note: some position activities require evening and weekend commitments. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position is performed partly on site and partly in a hybrid or remote environment. Work performed on site requires the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. Work performed in a hybrid or remote environment requires maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits Academic Services Intermediate Professional The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $53,000 – $57,000. Academic Services Senior Professional The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $55,000 – $59,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 30, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brigid Kane, brigid.kane@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    }
  },
